    "Video Game Music File",
    "3.6",
    "Audio file used by some Yamaha and Texas Instruments sound chips that were included with older video game systems; contains video game audio that can be synthesized by the sound chip; can be played with computer software that emulates the sound chip. NOTE: VGM files were used for game consoles such as the Sega Genesis, Sega Game Gear, and Capcom arcade machines. Windows Audio Overload. Nullsoft Winamp with Chipamp plug-in. Foobar2000 with vgmstream decoder plug-in. Mac Audio Overload. Linux Audio Overload. AudaciousFree.",
