    "WAVE Sound File",
    "3.6",
    "A WAVE file is a CD-quality audio file, similar to an.AIFF file. It stores an uncompressed audio waveform in a standardized format. WAVE files are more common on Windows systems, while AIFF files are more common on Macintosh computers. WAVE files most commonly use a.WAV extension. Windows Microsoft Windows Media Player Included with OS. Roxio Creator NXT Pro 9. Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Other audio player Mac Apple Music Included with OS. Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Roxio Toast 20. Other audio player.",
