    ["audio_files",
    ".H5E",
    "Line 6 POD HD500 Edit Preset File",
    "3.2",
    "Preset file created by Line 6 POD HD500 Edit, an instrument effects editing program; contains settings for FX, AMPS, Mixer, and Controllers that customize the sound of your instrument; different settings include drive, bass, treble, channel volume, parameters, tone, tempo sync, and speed. To create the H5E file, customize your settings, select File → Save As.., name the file, choose the save location, and click Save. To open the H5E file, double-click the file or select File → Open, navigate to the file, and click Open. In Mac, the default save location for H5E files is in the following directory: /​Documents/​Line 6/​Tones/​POD HD500 Edit In Windows, the default save location for H5E files is in the following directory: /​My Documents/​Line 6/​Tones/​POD HD500 Edit NOTE: The H5E extension was replaced by.5XE when POD HD500X Edit was released. Windows Line 6 POD HD500X Edit. Mac Line 6 POD HD500X Edit.",
    "Windows Line 6 POD HD500X Edit. Mac Line 6 POD HD500X Edit.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".TAK",
    "Music Maker Take File",
    "3.2",
    "Audio file created in the Toms lossless Audio Kompressor (TAK) format; uses an adaptive linear forward prediction technique to reduce the size of an audio file without losing audio quality; also supports non-audio data such as CD cover images or cue sheets. The TAK method of compression and decompression aims to provide higher compression ratios than other techniques while performing faster than other lossless compressors in benchmarks. The TAK format can be played back using plugins for Winamp and Foobar2000. TAK files can be compressed and decompressed using Tak, a program provided on the TAK development page. The downloaded package also includes the Winamp plugin and the TAK SDK. NOTE: The TAK homepage is written in German. Windows File Viewer Plus. Nullsoft Winamp with TAK plug-in. Foobar2000 with TAK Decoder plug-in. Tak. AIMP. VideoLAN VLC media player. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. Linux VideoLAN VLC media playerFree. Model file created by TAK (Thermal Analysis Kit) 2000, an engineering application used for analyzing the thermal characteristics of thermal systems; saves parameters for a thermal model, including nodes, conductors, and heat sources; used for generating output such as temperatures, heater statuses, and heat source information. TAK files are created in an ASCII text format. They are authored using a text editor and then run in TAK 2000. Windows K&K Associates TAK 2000. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor. Audio file created by Music Maker, a program used to make sounds, loops, and other music; stores an audio object (the core audio unit of the Music Maker software) plus all added effects; may store the sample duration, fade settings, and custom effects. Takes allow users to save edited audio samples without altering the original audio data. They can be created by selecting one or more objects and then choosing Edit → Object → Save objects as takes.. from the application menu. Windows MAGIX Music Maker 2022.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus. Nullsoft Winamp with TAK plug-in. Foobar2000 with TAK Decoder plug-in. Tak. AIMP. VideoLAN VLC media player. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. Windows K&K Associates TAK 2000. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor. Windows MAGIX Music Maker 2022.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".MX5",
    "Mixcraft 5 Audio Project",
    "3.2",
    "Audio project file created by Mixcraft 5, a multi-track software recording studio; can contain loops, imported audio, sound effects, and virtual instruments, as well as scored and edited video; used for creating musical compositions. Mixcraft 5 projects can be mixed down to.MP3,.OGG,.WMA, or.WAV files. Projects with video can be exported as.AVI and.WMV files. Windows Acoustica Mixcraft.",
    "Windows Acoustica Mixcraft.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".ODM",
    "OverDrive Media File",
    "3.2",
    "An ODM file is a master text document created by Apache OpenOffice Writer or another OpenDocument word processor. It contains several separate.ODT files that are joined together into one document. ODM files may also include a table of contents and an index. ODM file open in Apache OpenOffice Writer OpenOffice Writer is a free, open-source alternative to Microsoft Word. An OpenOffice Writer user who is producing a long document, such as a book, thesis, or report, may save that document as an ODM file. ODM files are master documents that allow users to save document sections, such as chapters and report sections, as separate documents (ODT files). Each section can then be edited separately and re-combined within the master document. The ability to edit a long document in sections is meant to improve users experience with OpenOffice Writer, because document sections load more quickly and are easier to work with than long documents. Since ODM files allow users to easily split, edit, and re-combine a documents sections, the ODM format is especially useful to those writing group documents. Each writer can edit their section as a separate document, before combining it within a single ODM file. NOTE: The Organization for the Advancement of Structured Information Standards (OASIS) maintains the OpenDocument standard. You can open an ODM file in OpenOffice Writer (cross-platform) or LibreOffice Writer (cross-platform). To do so, select File → Open.. from either programs menu bar and then open your ODM file. You can also use OpenOffice Writer to export an ODM file as a single ODT file, after youve finished editing the ODM file. To do so, select File → Export.. from the programs menu bar. Windows OpenOffice Writer. LibreOffice. Mac OpenOffice Writer. LibreOffice. Linux OpenOffice Writer. LibreOfficeFree. Media file shortcut to a file located in the Digital Library Reserve, such as an audio book, eBook, or music file; processed by the OverDrive Media Console, which will download the actual media file when the ODM file is opened. NOTE: OverDrive discontinued the Media Console app. Windows OverDrive Media Console —  (Discontinued). Mac OverDrive Media Console —  (Discontinued). iOS OverDrive Media Console —  (Discontinued). Android OverDrive Media Console —  (Discontinued). Chrome OS OverDrive Media Console —  (Discontinued).",
    "Windows OpenOffice Writer. LibreOffice. Mac OpenOffice Writer. LibreOffice. Linux OpenOffice Writer. LibreOffice. Windows OverDrive Media Console —  (Discontinued). Mac OverDrive Media Console —  (Discontinued). iOS OverDrive Media Console —  (Discontinued). Android OverDrive Media Console —  (Discontinued). Chrome OS OverDrive Media Console —  (Discontinued).",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".ADX",
    "ADX Audio File",
    "3.2",
    "Stores the indexing information for a Lotus Approach relational database. Windows IBM Lotus Approach (part of Lotus SmartSuite). An ADX file is an audio file used by various Sega Dreamcast, PlayStation 2, GameCube, and Wii video games. It is saved in the lossy ADX storage and compression format. ADX files are commonly used for background sounds because of their ability to loop. The ADX format can be found as an audio stream interleaved into.SFD Sofdec videos. Many of the Sonic the Hedgehog games, including the Sonic Mega Collection video game compilation, use ADX files for voice recordings and sounds. However, not many video games currently developed support the ADX format. NOTE: The FFmpeg supports ADX files but is limited to decoding 44100 Hz ADX files. Windows FFmpeg. Mac FFmpeg. Linux FFmpegFree.",
    "Windows IBM Lotus Approach (part of Lotus SmartSuite). Windows FFmpeg. Mac FFmpeg. Linux FFmpeg.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".MYR",
    "Myriad Music File",
    "3.2",
    "An MYR file is music file used by Myriad music applications such as Melody Assistant, Harmony Assistant, and Melody Player. It contains sheet music and instrumentation for a musical composition. MYR files can be played back in the software and exported to various audio formats, including.WAV,.MP3, and.MID. Windows Myriad Melody Assistant. Myriad Harmony Assistant. Myriad Melody Player. Mac Myriad Melody Assistant. Myriad Harmony Assistant. Myriad Melody Player. Linux Myriad Melody Assistant. Myriad Harmony Assistant.",
    "Windows Myriad Melody Assistant. Myriad Harmony Assistant. Myriad Melody Player. Mac Myriad Melody Assistant. Myriad Harmony Assistant. Myriad Melody Player. Linux Myriad Melody Assistant. Myriad Harmony Assistant.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".UWF",
    "UltraTracker Wave File",
    "3.2",
    "Audio waveform file used to store audio samples for the UltraTracker audio tracking program. Mac CocoModX —  (Discontinued). Windows UltraTracker.",
    "Mac CocoModX —  (Discontinued). Windows UltraTracker.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".GIO",
    "Adagio Score",
    "3.2",
    "A GIO file is a musical score written in the Adagio score language and supported by the Mandriva Nyquist score composition software. It contains the sheet music for a musical composition and includes MIDI data, instruments, notes, the composer and title, and other score information. Mandriva Nyquist is a discontinued score composition application for the also-discontinued Mandriva Linux distribution. When saving a score with Nyquist, the app creates a GIO file to store its contents. After saving the musical score, you can close it, then re-open it to continue modifying the score. The Adagio score language saved in GIO files consists of text commands that specify each note in the score, with each note consisting of one or several of the following attributes: Time Pitch Loudness Duration Articulation Voice number Tempo Rate. You can open a GIO file with Mandriva Nyquist. However, the software is discontinued. Since GIO files store information in plain text, you can also view and edit the score with a text editor, such as Microsoft Notepad (Windows) or Apple TextEdit (Mac). Windows Any text editor Mac Any text editor Linux Mandriva Nyquist Any text editor. Musical score written in the Nyquist score language; processed using a Lisp interpreter; used for sound synthesis and music composition. Linux Mandriva Nyquist.",
    "Windows Any text editor. Mac Any text editor. Linux Mandriva Nyquist Any text editor. Linux Mandriva Nyquist.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".AXA",
    "Annodex Audio File",
    "3.2",
    "Audio file stored in the Annodex format, which is similar to the Ogg container format; contains compressed audio, along with Continuous Media Markup Language (CMML) and codec information to make it easier for the content to be searched and accessed. The audio in the AXA file may be compressed by a variety of codecs, such as Vorbis, FLAC, Speex, or Ghost. NOTE: The Annodex plugin for the Mozilla Firefox web browser is no longer available. Windows VideoLAN VLC media player. Mac Macgo Mac Media Player. VideoLAN VLC media player. Linux VideoLAN VLC media playerFree.",
    "Windows VideoLAN VLC media player. Mac Macgo Mac Media Player. VideoLAN VLC media player. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".MUSX",
    "Finale Notation File ",
    "3.2",
    "A MUSX file is a musical score created by MakeMusic Finale, a popular scorewriting program. It contains musical notation, including measures, notes, time signatures, tempos, and clefs. It likely also includes a title, composer information, and copyright information. MUSX file open in MakeMusic Finale Composers use MakeMusic Finale to create, edit, and listen to musical scores. For example, a composer might use Finale to compose a new version of Auld Lang Syne, add lyrics to the score, and play the score back via their computers speakers to check for errors. Finale 2014 and later versions save the scores that composers create as MUSX files. In addition to the score a composer has created, each MUSX file contains MIDI data that Finale uses when playing back the score. NOTE: Finale 2012 and earlier versions save scores as.MUS files. You can open a MUSX file with MakeMusic Finale (Windows, Mac). To do so, select File → Open.. from the programs menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your MUSX file. You can also open a MUSX file with MakeMusic SmartMusic (Windows, Mac) and MakeMusic Finale PrintMusic (Windows). Windows MakeMusic Finale. MakeMusic SmartMusic. MakeMusic Finale PrintMusic. Mac MakeMusic Finale. MakeMusic SmartMusic.",
    "Windows MakeMusic Finale. MakeMusic SmartMusic. MakeMusic Finale PrintMusic. Mac MakeMusic Finale. MakeMusic SmartMusic.",
    "You can use MakeMusic Finale to export the score a MUSX file contains in a variety of formats, including:.MUS - Finale 2012 Score.AIFF - Audio Interchange File Format.WAV - WAVE Audio.EPUB - Open eBook.MIDI - MIDI Music Data.MXL - Compressed MusicXML."],
    ["audio_files",
    ".MMM",
    "Music Maker Arrangement File",
    "3.2",
    "An MMM file is an audio project created by MAGIX Music Maker, a digital audio workstation (DAW). It contains a multitrack arrangement, which includes instrumental loops, audio clips, transitions, and effects. MMM file open in MAGIX Music Maker 2019 MMM files allow you to save, close, and reopen an arrangement project for further editing. When you are finished fine-tuning your arrangement, you can export your arrangement to several different audio formats, including.WAV,.MP3,.OGG,.WMA, and.MOV. You can open an MMM file in Music Maker by selecting File → Load project.. or by clicking the folder icon in the menu. You can save an MMM file in Music Maker by selecting File → Save project.. or by clicking the floppy disk icon in the menu. Windows MAGIX Music Maker 2022. Data file introduced with version 7 of Money Manager, a personal and business finance application; stores financial data for bank accounts, orders, and transactions; used for tracking personal or company finances and can be used for generating reports in the software. NOTE: Money Manager version 6 uses.MM6 files. Windows Moneysoft Money Manager. Uncompressed maps file created with MiraMon, a Geographic Information Systems (GIS) program developed cooperatively by the Centre for Ecological Research and Forestry Applications (CREAF) and the University of Barcelona (UAB); contains graphical map data in both vector and raster formats; may also include attached documents or media files. MiraMon Maps can be compressed into.MMZ files to make them easier to distribute. In order to access individual layers of the map file it must be viewed in the uncompressed format. Windows MiraMon. MiraMon Universal Map ReaderFree. Resource file created for Multiple Master Fonts, which are Type 1 font programs that include two or more master fonts within a single font file; contains metric data referenced by.PFM and.PFB files in the Windows Environment; not meant to be manually opened. The data held in MMM files determine the font axes, which represent the width, weight, and optical size of the font. NOTE: Must be used with PFM and PFB font files. Windows Microsoft Windows Font Viewer Included with OS.",
    "Windows MAGIX Music Maker 2022. Windows Moneysoft Money Manager. Windows MiraMon. MiraMon Universal Map Reader. Windows Microsoft Windows Font Viewer Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".NVF",
    "Creative Labs NVF Audio File",
    "3.2",
    "Voice audio file recorded using some of Creative Labs MP3 players; stores audio in Creatives proprietary NOMAD II Voice Format (NVF), which uses G.721 mono Adaptive Differential Pulse-Code Modulation (ADPCM); used for storing voice recordings, such as personal memos, on Creative devices. NVF files can be played in iTunes, or using Creatives NOMAD II Manager software. Windows Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Creative Labs NOMAD II Manager Mac Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Linux NVFToolsFree.",
    "Windows Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Creative Labs NOMAD II Manager. Mac Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Linux NVFTools.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".SID",
    "SID Audio File",
    "3.2",
    "Backup file created by Steam, an application used to download and manage Valve video games on desktop computers; contains compressed game data created by the Steam backup feature (steambackup.exe program); used to backup games to DVDs or other external media. SID files are created with a.SIS file and a.SIM file, which provide metadata necessary to restore backup game data. SID files use the naming convention {game}_disk{X}_{Y}.sid, where game is the name of the backup game, X is the disk number, and Y is the backup file number on the disk. NOTE: Steam backups do not include saved games, custom multiplayer maps, or configuration files. You must backup and restore those files manually. Windows Valve Steam. Mac Valve Steam. Image created using Multi-resolution Seamless Image Database (MrSID) compression, which was developed by Extensis for compressing large images; commonly used to partition and store large Geographic Information Systems (GIS) images. NOTE: Extensis was formerly known as LizardTech. Windows Extensis GeoExpress. Extensis GeoViewer. Extensis Express Server. Extensis SquishPic. ESRI ArcGIS Pro. ERDAS IMAGINE. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. A Web browser with LizardTech ExpressView (MrSID) Browser Plug-in Mac Extensis SquishPic. A Web browser with LizardTech ExpressView (MrSID) Browser Plug-in Linux Extensis Express Server. Extensis SquishPic. Audio file originally used by Commodore computer systems, but now more often used for playing the sounds on Commodore emulators and SID software players; often used for video game background music and can use mono or stereo audio formats; created for the MOS Technology 6502 processor, which can be emulated by newer desktop software to play the audio. SID files may use the PSID format or the newer RSID (Real SID) format. While the PSID format is more compatible with general Commodore emulation software, the RSID format requires more complete emulation of the C64 hardware. Windows ACID 64 Player. quadraSID. Mac SIDPLAY. quadraSID. Linux Audacious. SIDPlayerFree. Document created and used by ScanIt, an application used to extract data from graphs; contains the graph image and its metadata; includes axes definitions, document windows, and other document specific options. The SID file allows you to save your progress and continue it at a later time. The file can be saved to a variety of image formats, such as.JPEG,.PNG,.TIF, and.BMP. Windows AmsterCHEM ScanItFree.",
    "Windows Valve Steam. Mac Valve Steam. Windows Extensis GeoExpress. Extensis GeoViewer. Extensis Express Server. Extensis SquishPic. ESRI ArcGIS Pro. ERDAS IMAGINE. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. A Web browser with LizardTech ExpressView (MrSID) Browser Plug-in. Mac Extensis SquishPic. A Web browser with LizardTech ExpressView (MrSID) Browser Plug-in. Linux Extensis Express Server. Extensis SquishPic. Windows ACID 64 Player. quadraSID. Mac SIDPLAY. quadraSID. Linux Audacious. SIDPlayer. Windows AmsterCHEM ScanIt.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".XSP",
    "Kodi Smart Playlist File",
    "3.2",
    "Song or video playlist used by Kodi, a free software multimedia player; may contain a list of specific audio and video files to play, or may store criteria for the types of media to play (e.g., play Rock music or all 90s music); can specify songs, albums, movies, TV shows, and other types of media. XSP files should be placed in the Userdata directory for the Kodi installation for them to be read by the program. XSP files use an XML text format. Therefore, you can create them with any text editor and then place them in the Userdata directory. NOTE: Kodi was previously known as XBMC. Android Kodi. Windows Kodi. Any text editor Mac Kodi. Any text editor Linux Kodi. Any text editor iOS KodiFree.",
    "Android Kodi. Windows Kodi. Any text editor. Mac Kodi. Any text editor. Linux Kodi. Any text editor. iOS Kodi.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".SAMPLE",
    "Godot Engine Wav Audio File",
    "3.2",
    "A SAMPLE file is an audio file created by Godot Engine, a free and open source game engine used to create 2D and 3D games. It stores audio in a format similar to the Waveform audio file format (WAV) but includes a custom header. SAMPLE files are created when a user imports a.WAV file to be used in a game for sound effects, background music, or narration. Godot Engine also creates.OGGSTR files when.OGG files are imported into a game project. Windows Godot Engine. Mac Godot Engine. Linux Godot EngineFree.",
    "Windows Godot Engine. Mac Godot Engine. Linux Godot Engine.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".XP",
    "Fasttracker 2 Extended Pattern",
    "3.2",
    "An XP file is a song pattern created by the Starbreeze Studios Fasttracker 2, an audio tracker for MS-DOS. It stores a pattern, which consists of multiple rows (64 by default and 1,024 maximum) divided into columns configuring aspects of the note (instrument used, volume setting, effects, etc.). Fasttracker 2 users can arrange patterns in XP files with other patterns to create a complete song, or.XM module. Fasttracker 2, or Fasttracker II, is an audio tracker designed for creating music. You can arrange patterns (stored in XP files) along a master timeline to create a sequence that makes up a song. Starbreeze Studios is a Swedish start-up that developed and released Fasttracker 2 in November 1994. The company developed the software through version 2.08, releasing it in August 1997. You can open an XP file with Starbreeze Studios Fasttracker in Windows. Windows Starbreeze Studios Fasttracker 2Free. Game file used by XPilot, an older 2D space fighting game; saved in a plain text format and saves the map features and obstacles as a 2D grid; also saves gameplay properties for the map. Windows XPilot. Linux XPilotFree.",
    "Windows Starbreeze Studios Fasttracker 2. Windows XPilot. Linux XPilot.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".VPR",
    "VOCALOID5 Project File",
    "3.2",
    "A VPR file is a project file created by YAMAHA VOCALOID5 or VOCALOID6. It contains a record of the musical notes, lyrics, and synthesized vocals the project contains. The VPR format was introduced with the release of VOCALOID5 and replaced the.VSQX format. Musicians use YAMAHA VOCALOID to create synthesized vocal tracks, comprised of notes, lyrics, and synthesized singing voices. Different versions of VOCALOID save users vocal-creation projects in different formats. VOCALOID5 and VOCALOID6 save users projects as VPR files. Previous versions of VOCALOID saved projects as VSQX and.VSQ files. While VOCALOID5 and VOCALOID6 no longer save projects as VSQX files, they can still load projects saved in the VSQX format. When a user saves one of these projects in VOCALOID5 or VOCALOID6, the program converts the project to the VPR format. You can open a VPR file with YAMAHA VOCALOID5 or VOCALOID6. Both programs are available for Windows and macOS. Mac YAMAHA VOCALOID5. YAMAHA VOCALOID6. Windows YAMAHA VOCALOID5. YAMAHA VOCALOID6.",
    "Mac YAMAHA VOCALOID5. YAMAHA VOCALOID6. Windows YAMAHA VOCALOID5. YAMAHA VOCALOID6.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".DS2",
    "Olympus DSS Pro Audio File",
    "3.2",
    "Audio file created in the Digital Speech Standard Pro (DS2) format, a highly compressed audio format developed by Olympus for digital voice recordings; typically contains a recording of human speech that is saved to a recording devices memory card; used for saving personal and professional notes, often by laywers, researchers, and physicians; useful for sending as email attachments because of the highly compressed file size. DS2 files can be converted to standard.WAV files using DSS Player Pro, a software application included with some Olympus digital voice recorder purchases. DS2 files can also be converted with DSS File Converter from Voelker Software. NOTE: Example Olympus devices that create DS2 files include the DS-2400, DS-4000, and DS-5000. Windows Olympus DSS Player. Voelker Software DSS File Converter. Bytescribe WavPlayer. NCH WavePad.",
    "Windows Olympus DSS Player. Voelker Software DSS File Converter. Bytescribe WavPlayer. NCH WavePad.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".MPGA",
    "MPEG-1 Layer 3 Audio File",
    "3.2",
    "Compressed audio file encoded with MPEG-1 Layer 3 compression; compresses the audio using lossy compression that maintains most of the original sound quality. MPGA files are basically.MP3 files with a different file extension. Windows Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Microsoft Windows Media Player Included with OS. RealNetworks RealPlayer 20/20. Any audio player that supports MP3 files Mac Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Any audio player that supports MP3 files Linux Any audio player that supports MP3 files iOS RealNetworks RealTimes: Video Maker. Android RealNetworks RealTimes Video Maker.",
    "Windows Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Microsoft Windows Media Player Included with OS. RealNetworks RealPlayer 20/20. Any audio player that supports MP3 files. Mac Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Any audio player that supports MP3 files. Linux Any audio player that supports MP3 files. iOS RealNetworks RealTimes: Video Maker. Android RealNetworks RealTimes Video Maker.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".PSF",
    "Portable Sound File",
    "3.2",
    "Preference file that stores color settings used by Photoshop to provide accurate previews of how images will look when they are printed; can be loaded by selecting View → Proof Setup → Custom.. in Photoshop. In Windows, PSF files are stored in the following directory:~/​Application Data/​Adobe/​Color/​Proofing. In Mac OS X, they are stored in the following folder: ~/​Library/​Application Support/​Adobe/​Color/​Proofing. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe Photoshop Elements. Windows Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe Photoshop Elements. Sound file saved in the Portable Sound Format (PSF); designed to bring earlier gaming sound formats to next-generation consoles; uses the music driver code from the original game, which allows the sound to be authentically reproduced. PSF includes the following sub-formats: PSF1 - Playstation PSF2 - Playstation 2 SSF - Saturn (under development) DSF - Dreamcast (under development) USF - Nintendo 64 (developed by Adam Gashlin) GSF - GameBoy Advance (developed by Caitsith2 and Zoopd) QSF - Capcom QSound PSF files can be played back on a PC using common audio programs with supporting plugins. Mac Audio Overload. Windows Audio Overload. Nullsoft Winamp with the Highly Experimental plugin. XMPlay with the Highly Experimental plugin. Linux Audio OverloadFree. Font information file used by AutoCAD, a CAD engineering design and documentation application; stores font substitution information used when exporting a drawing to a PostScript file; allows users to customize font styles in printed or published drawings. The default PostScript pattern file for AutoCAD has the filename acad.psf. AutoCAD LTs PSF file has the name aclt.psf. Windows Autodesk AutoCAD 2023. Text file that defines an HP-UX software package; used by the SD-UX swpackage session and identifies the contents, attributes, compatibilities, and dependencies of the product. The PSF is used for the following purposes: Define vendor information Specify one or more products Define attributes for one or more files, filesets, and subproducts Define attributes for the distribution media Specify what computers and operating systems the product supports Define descriptive attributes of the software objects. Linux HP Software Distributor. Support file used by GPS software; contains the root mean square (RMS) values of ephemeris components, which define the positions of celestial objects; also includes the clock time for each tracked satellite over the past seven days. Prediction support files are used to determine how individual satellites are performing. They can also be used to calculate statistical estimates of long term GPS accuracy. Windows GIANT. Bitmap image format used by PhotoStudio, an image-editing program; supports text, shapes, and multiple layers; commonly used for saving edited digital photos. ArcSoft PhotoStudio for Canon is commonly included with Canon digital cameras. PSF files can also be opened by ArcSoft PhotoImpression, which has been discontinued. They may be opened with Adobe Photoshop by changing the extension from .psf to .jpg. However, other image-editing programs may still not be able to open the file. NOTE: PhotoStudio has been discontinued and is no longer supported by ArcSoft. Mac ArcSoft PhotoStudio Windows ArcSoft PhotoStudio. Output file generated by SPI Proxy, a proxy server tool included with SPI Dynamics SPI ToolKit; records and logs details of traffic passing through the proxy server; saved in a proprietary format readable only by SPI software. SPI Dynamics was acquired by HP on August 1, 2007. Windows SPI Dynamics WebInspect Toolkit. Parameter ID (PID) script used by OBD-II scanner software; allows the software to retrieve error codes and status information from an automobiles OBD (On-Board Diagnostic) device; can be imported with the PMSCAN diagnostic tool. Windows Palmer Performance PMSCAN.",
    "Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe Photoshop Elements. Windows Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe Photoshop Elements. Mac Audio Overload. Windows Audio Overload. Nullsoft Winamp with the Highly Experimental plugin. XMPlay with the Highly Experimental plugin. Linux Audio Overload. Windows Autodesk AutoCAD 2023. Linux HP Software Distributor. Windows GIANT. Mac ArcSoft PhotoStudio. Windows ArcSoft PhotoStudio. Windows SPI Dynamics WebInspect Toolkit. Windows Palmer Performance PMSCAN.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".ADT",
    "ADTS Audio File",
    "3.1",
    "An ADT file is a template for creating a new word processing document in ACT! contact management software. It is used for creating multiple documents with a similar layout. ADT files may be created with a third-party word processor, such as Microsoft Word, which works in conjunction with ACT!. The default location for storing ADT files is C:/Program Files/ACT/Templates. NOTE: Sage ACT! became Swiftpage Act! in 2013. Windows Swiftpage Act!. Map file used by World of Warcraft (WoW), a massively-multiplayer online role-playing game (MMORPG); contains a map tile for a game continent or dungeon; used for loading map terrain and objects while playing the game. ADT files are included inside.MPQ archives, which are used for game installation data and updates. WoW updates may include ADT files to change map contents. Example ADT filenames include Northrend_33_18.adt, Azeroth_29_47.adt, and IcecrownCitadel_25_28.adt. Windows Blizzard World of Warcraft. Mac Blizzard World of Warcraft. Audio file encoded in the Audio Data Transport Stream (ADTS) format; contains a series of audio frames, each of which includes a portion of the overall audio data to be transferred; commonly used for streaming.AAC audio; also seen with the.ADTS extension. Windows Microsoft Groove Music Included with OS. Microsoft Windows Media Player Included with OS. VideoLAN VLC media player. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. Linux VideoLAN VLC media playerFree. Log file generated by AutoCAD, a common 2D and 3D CAD program; records the activity that occurs during a drawing audit. To create an ADT file within AutoCAD, follow these steps. Begin a drawing audit (File Menu→Drawing Utilities→Audit). On the command line, type auditctl. Enter 1 (instead of the default value of 0). Press the Enter key. The audit log will then be created in the same directory as the current drawing with the filename drawing.adt.. Windows Autodesk AutoCAD 2023. View in a text editor.",
    "Windows Swiftpage Act!. Windows Blizzard World of Warcraft. Mac Blizzard World of Warcraft. Windows Microsoft Groove Music Included with OS. Microsoft Windows Media Player Included with OS. VideoLAN VLC media player. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. Windows Autodesk AutoCAD 2023. View in a text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".WV",
    "WavPack Audio File",
    "3.1",
    "A WV file is an audio file compressed using WavPack Hybrid Lossless Compression. WavPack supports both lossy and lossless compression, which produces high-quality compressed files. WV files compression ratio is typically between 30% and 70%. WavPack compression supports mono, stereo, and multichannel audio. It is compatible with most PCM audio formats including 8, 16, 24, and 32-bit recordings, and supports sampling rates from 6 to 192 kHz. You can open and play a WV file using a variety of media players, such as VLC media player (cross-platform), VUPlayer (Windows), X Lossless Decoder (Mac), and Aqualung (Linux). You can also use X Lossless Decoder and Adobe Audition (with the WavPack plugin installed) to convert WV files to other audio formats. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. WavPack Win32. Foobar2000. VUPlayer. Cockos REAPER. Image-Line FL Studio. Lightning UK! ImgBurn. Adobe Audition with WavPack plugin. Nullsoft Winamp with WavPack plugin. Steinberg WaveLab with WavPack plugin. Media Player Classic. VideoLAN VLC media player. Mac X Lossless Decoder. VideoLAN VLC media player. Max. Linux WavPack for Linux. Aqualung. Audacious. VideoLAN VLC media playerFree.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. WavPack Win32. Foobar2000. VUPlayer. Cockos REAPER. Image-Line FL Studio. Lightning UK! ImgBurn. Adobe Audition with WavPack plugin. Nullsoft Winamp with WavPack plugin. Steinberg WaveLab with WavPack plugin. Media Player Classic. VideoLAN VLC media player. Mac X Lossless Decoder. VideoLAN VLC media player. Max. Linux WavPack for Linux. Aqualung. Audacious. VideoLAN VLC media player.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".XM",
    "Fasttracker 2 Extended Module",
    "3.1",
    "An XM file is a music module created by Fasttracker 2, an audio tracker program. It contains MIDI data and sound samples that comprise a song. XM files are similar to.S3M and.MOD files but are saved in the Fasttracker Extended Module (XM) format. XM file open in OpenMPT 1 Fasttracker 2, or Fasttracker II, is a music tracker released in the 1990s for MS-DOS by Fredrik Huss and Magnus Högdahl but it is no longer developed. The software allows you to create music by arranging patterns of samples in tracks. When saving a composition, Fasttracker 2, creates an XM file to store the music. While Fasttracker 2 was discontinued in the 1990s, people may still export modules to the XM format with other applications. You can open an XM file with various audio trackers and media players, including OpenMPT (Windows), Nullsoft Winamp (Windows), and VideoLAN VLC media player (multiplatform). For example, to open an XM file with OpenMPT, select File → Open. Windows OpenMPT. XMPlay. MilkyTracker. Nullsoft Winamp. FMJ-Software Awave Studio. VideoLAN VLC media player. CoolUtils Total Audio Converter. MikMod. Mac CocoModX —  (Discontinued). MilkyTracker. PlayerPro —  (Discontinued). XimpleMOD. VideoLAN VLC media player. MikMod. Linux MilkyTracker. VideoLAN VLC media player. MikModFree.",
    "Windows OpenMPT. XMPlay. MilkyTracker. Nullsoft Winamp. FMJ-Software Awave Studio. VideoLAN VLC media player. CoolUtils Total Audio Converter. MikMod. Mac CocoModX —  (Discontinued). MilkyTracker. PlayerPro —  (Discontinued). XimpleMOD. VideoLAN VLC media player. MikMod. Linux MilkyTracker. VideoLAN VLC media player. MikMod.",
    "Various programs, such as OpenMPT and MilkyTracker, can convert XM files to other file types. For example, OpenMPT can convert XM files to the following formats:.MPTM - OpenMPT Module.MID - MIDI File.IT - Impulse Tracker Module.WAV - WAVE Audio File.FLAC -. Lossless Audio Codec File.AU - Audacity Audio File.OPUS - Opus Audio File.OGG - Ogg Vorbis Audio File.RAW - Raw Audio Data.MP3 - MP3 Audio File."],
    ["audio_files",
    ".M4P",
    "iTunes Music Store Audio File",
    "3.1",
    "Protected.AAC audio file downloaded from the iTunes Music Store; incorporates Apple Computers Fairplay DRM copy protection, which limits the number of computers the file can be played on. In order to play a protected M4P file, you must authorize your computer using Apple iTunes. This is done by entering a username and password for the account that downloaded the file. Up to five computers can be authorized with the same account. Windows Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Mac Apple Music Included with OS. Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS.",
    "Windows Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Mac Apple Music Included with OS. Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".PD",
    "Spore Audio Playback File",
    "3.1",
    "A PD file is a design created by FlexiSIGN 5, a program used to professionally design, print, and cut signs. It contains a graphic design of a sign in a vector graphic format so that the image can be resized without losing quality. PD files may also store raster graphics and text. Signs and banners stored in PD files can be opened by FlexiSIGN. The design can then be printed on a wide format printer and cut by a vinyl cutter. FlexiSIGN can also connect to a print and cut all-in-one machine. If you want to share PD files with another person that does not own FlexiSIGN, you can convert your PD files. FlexiSIGN allows you to export your designs to the more widely supported JPEG and PDF formats. NOTE: SAi FlexiSIGN was renamed SAi Flexi. Windows SAi Flexi. Mac SAi Flexi. A PD file is a Pure Data (Pd) file used by Spore, a creature evolution and survival video game. Spores PD files are stored within the games audio.PACKAGE files. They specify how background music plays and loops. Pure Data is a visual programming language that developers can use to create interactive computer music. Electronic Arts has created their own version of Pure Data, called EAPd, which is embedded into Spore. EAPd uses PD files to play in-game music. Spore PD files are plain text files, so you can open and edit them in any text editor, such as Microsoft Notepad (Windows), Apple TextEdit (Mac), or GitHub Atom (cross-platform). Windows Electronic Arts Spore. Any text editor Mac Electronic Arts Spore. Any text editor. A PD file is a patch used by the Pure Data visual programming environment. It contains a program that can be opened in a Pure Data environment and used to create music or other multimedia. PD files are plain text files, so you can also open them and view their contents in any text editor. PD file open in Pure Data Pure Data (Pd) is a visual programming language and environment that developers can use to develop interactive music-creation programs. To create a Pd program, developers connect Pd objects together. Each object typically controls some aspect of the audio that the program produces, such as the audios frequency or volume. Pd programs are referred to as patches, and they are saved as PD files. PD files can contain any number of objects. They may also contain comments about how to use the program the PD file contains. When viewed in a text editor, PD files contents appear as a series of lines of text. These lines of text define the canvas, objects, and other items that appear in Pd. Each line of text begins with a # combined with a letter (such as #N, #X, or #A) and ends with a semicolon. PD files are meant to be opened as Pure Data patches. To open a PD file in the default version of Pd, select File → Open from the programs menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your PD file. You can also open a PD file as a plain text document in any text editor, to review the Pd code it contains. Windows Pure Data. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor Mac Pure Data. Apple TextEdit Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor Linux Pure Data. Vim. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor Chrome OS Google Chrome Text Included with OS.",
    "Windows SAi Flexi. Mac SAi Flexi. Windows Electronic Arts Spore. Any text editor. Mac Electronic Arts Spore. Any text editor. Windows Pure Data. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. Mac Pure Data. Apple TextEdit Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. Linux Pure Data. Vim. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. Chrome OS Google Chrome Text Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".MMP",
    "MixMeister Playlist",
    "3.1",
    "Master Album Maker project file, which includes the album structure, text, effects, and links to all the pictures and audio files referenced by the album. Windows Intrepid Mouse Master Album Maker. Playlist of songs for MixMeister DJ mixing software; contains references to the songs, but not the actual songs themselves. Windows MixMeister Technology MixMeister. Project file used by Symbian OS development tools; contains project properties used to build the project regardless of the platform or compiler being used; used by the Symbian SDKs makmake or abld tools to convert the file into a makefile for a specific platform. MMP files may contain references to targets, source code files to be compiled, include directories, and application resources. NOTE: Nokia Symbian SDK is no longer available. Windows Nokia Symbian SDK. Data file created by MindManager, an application used for developing and organizing ideas visually; created by the Windows version of MindManager and cannot be opened on Mac versions of the software. Mindjet replaced MMP files with.MMAP files. No programs available. An MMP file is a video editing project created in EffectMatrix MovieMator Video Editor Pro, a video editing program available for Windows and macOS. It contains XML-formatted text used to load a project in MovieMator Video Editor Pro. MMP files can be used to create.MP4,.FLV,.AVI, and.MOV videos. MMP file open in File Viewer MovieMator Video Editor Pro is a video editing program that amateur video editors can use to create edited videos. The application allows editors to import video and audio clips, edit clips and splice them together along Video Editor Pros timeline, and add images, animations, and other visual effects to their videos. When an editor saves a MovieMator Video Editor Pro video editing project, the project is saved as an MMP file. Though MMP files are used to open projects in MovieMator Video Editor Pro, they do not contain any video, audio, or image assets. Instead, MMP files contain XML-formatted text that MovieMator Video Editor Pro reads to load video editing projects. Most notably, MMP files contain references to the locations at which the video, audio, and image assets used in a project are stored. If an editor moves an asset from the location referenced in their MMP file, the file will not load correctly in MovieMator Video Editor Pro. After an editor finishes editing their video, they can export it as an MP4, FLV, AVI, MOV, or other type of video file. Editors can either manually select the type of video file they want to export their video as, or they can select the device or website their video is intended to be used with. If an editor selects a device or website, MovieMator Video Editor Pro will export the editors video in a format optimized for that device or website. You can open an MMP file (MovieMator Video Editor Pro Project) in MovieMator Video Editor Pro (Windows, Mac). To do so, select File → Open File.. from the programs menu bar. Windows EffectMatrix MovieMator Video Editor Pro. Mac EffectMatrix MovieMator Video Editor Pro. Project created by LMMS (Linux MultiMedia Studio), a music creation program; contains LMMS project data such as track edits, tempo, pitch, volume, and included instrument types; can be exported as.WAV and.OGG audio files. To create the MMP file, click the save icon in the top-left of the application or select Project → Save or Save As.., name your project, choose the save location, and click Save. To open the MMP file, you can simply double-click the file. You can also open the project inside of the application, select Project → Open.., navigate to your file, select it, and click Open. NOTE: LMMS replaced the MMP file extension with the.MMPZ extension. Windows LMMS. Mac LMMS. Linux LMMSFree.",
    "Windows Intrepid Mouse Master Album Maker. Windows MixMeister Technology MixMeister. Windows Nokia Symbian SDK No programs available Windows EffectMatrix MovieMator Video Editor Pro. Mac EffectMatrix MovieMator Video Editor Pro. Windows LMMS. Mac LMMS. Linux LMMS.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".A2M",
    "Adlib Tracker II File",
    "3.1",
    "Configuration file that stores preferences for TS-AudioToMIDI, an audio to MIDI conversion program; can be opened or saved within the program by clicking the Open Settings or Save Settings buttons at the bottom of main window. The A2M file contains settings for the following options: Tune, Auto Tune, Threshold, Noise Gate, Selectivity, Sharpness, MIDI Instrument, MIDI channel, Transpose, Algorithm, Minimal Note, and Pause duration. Settings for the Equalizer (EQ), Filter, and Harmonic model are also saved. Windows TallStick Software TS-AudioToMIDI. Sound module created with Adlib Tracker II, an audio tracking program; may contain multiple tracks with musical scores that play back sound samples contained within the file. NOTE: Adlib Tracker II is a DOS program but should run on any Windows platform. Windows Nullsoft Winamp with AdPlug plugin. Adlib Tracker IIFree.",
    "Windows TallStick Software TS-AudioToMIDI. Windows Nullsoft Winamp with AdPlug plugin. Adlib Tracker II.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".AVASTSOUNDS",
    "Avast Soundpack File",
    "3.1",
    "An AVASTSOUNDS file is an audio pack used by Avast antivirus and internet protection software. It stores a collection of.WAV sound files the software plays when certain events occur in the software, such as a threat detection or completion of a virus scan. Many soundpacks are available for download at the Avast website. Often these themes have humorous human speech audio, such as Redneck or Santa Claus voices. The audio packs are also available in multiple languages. NOTE: Avast discontinued Pro Antivirus and Internet Security, and its software no longer utilizes AVASTSOUNDS files. You can open an AVASTSOUNDS file by double-clicking the file (as long as the Avast software is already installed). After double-clicking the file, the Avast software installs the sound pack. Windows Avast Pro Antivirus Avast Internet Security.",
    "Windows Avast Pro Antivirus Avast Internet Security.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".EAR",
    "Eyemail Audio Recording",
    "3.1",
    "An EAR file is an application archive used by Java EE (Enterprise Edition), a platform used for programming server-side software such as web applications. It contains.JAR and.WAR files, which together comprise a Java EE application package. EAR files are used for running the application on a Java EE-enabled server, such as GlassFish Server or Geronimo. EAR files are similar to.JAR files, but they are packaged for Java EE instead of the Java SE (Standard Edition). Both JAR and EAR files use.ZIP compression, which means you can use Zip decompression programs, such as 7-Zip, to unpack the contents of the files. NOTE: Java EE application are developed using the Java EE SDK, which can be downloaded from Oracles website. Java EE adds additional features to Java SE for server programming. Windows Oracle GlassFish Server. Apache Geronimo. IBM WebSphere Application Server. 7-Zip. Mac Oracle GlassFish Server. Apache Geronimo. Linux Oracle GlassFish Server. Apache Geronimo. IBM WebSphere Application Server. An EAR file is an audio file saved in the Eyemail Audio Recording (EAR) format developed by Eyemail Technology Inc. (ETI). The format was primarily used to store recorded audio in the 2000s by Camcorder 2, a video recording program for Nokia mobile phones. The EAR format is related to the.EYE video format that ETI also develops. EAR files are obscure since ETI discontinued the EAR format, and Nokia phones no longer save audio as EAR files. However, you may still encounter EAR files if you recorded audio with a Nokia phone, then transferred the EAR files to your computer. You can play EAR files with ETI Monet TV in Windows. However, ETI discontinued the software. No other known program supports EAR files. Windows ETI Monet TV —  (Discontinued).",
    "Windows Oracle GlassFish Server. Apache Geronimo. IBM WebSphere Application Server. 7-Zip. Mac Oracle GlassFish Server. Apache Geronimo. Linux Oracle GlassFish Server. Apache Geronimo. IBM WebSphere Application Server. Windows ETI Monet TV —  (Discontinued).",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".BMML",
    "Braille Music Markup Language File",
    "3.1",
    "A BMML file is a mockup file created by Balsamiq Mockups, an application used to build GUI designs and website wireframes. It contains markup language in XML format that is rendered into a mockup of a user interface when opened in Balsamiq Mockups. BMML files were replaced by BMPR files, which are saved in binary format. A mockup consists of various assets, buttons, containers, forms, icons, text, media, and symbols used for designing a user interface or website. Balsamiq Mockups originally stored mockups in.XML files then introduced BMML files in version 2 of the program. BMML files are simply XML files with the .bmml extension. However, BMML files were then replaced by BMPR files with the release of Balsamiq Mockups 3. NOTE: You can still import BMML files into Balsamiq Mockups by selecting Project → Import. Windows Balsamiq Mockups. Mac Balsamiq Mockups. File saved in the BMML format and opened by Braille Music Reader, a music creation tool for visually impaired persons; contains a braille musical score; includes score data, such as notes, pitch, and octaves. To open a BMML file in Braille Music Reader, select File → Import → Bmml, navigate to your file, and click Open. Windows Braille Music ReaderFree.",
    "Windows Balsamiq Mockups. Mac Balsamiq Mockups. Windows Braille Music Reader.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".5XB",
    "Line 6 POD HD500X Edit Bundle",
    "3.1",
    "Bundle file created by Line 6 POD HD500X Edit, a DAW program that enables you to edit and create instrument sound effects; contains up to 8 setlists with presets; once loaded, will change the settings for FX, AMPS, Mixer, and Controllers, which create different sounds from your interment depending on how you customize them. To create the 5XB file, customize your settings, select File → Save Bundle As.., name the file, choose the save location, and click Save. To open the 5XB file, double-click the file or select File → Open Bundle.., navigate to the file, and click Open. In Windows, the default save location for 5XB files is in the following directory: /​My Documents/​Line 6/​Tones/​POD HD500X Edit/​Bundles In Mac, the default save location for 5XB files is in the following directory: /​Documents/​Line 6/​Tones/​POD HD500X Edit/​Bundles NOTE: When POD HD500X Edit was released, the 5XB extension replaced the.H5B extension, which was used by POD HD500 Edit. Windows Line 6 POD HD500X Edit. Mac Line 6 POD HD500X Edit.",
    "Windows Line 6 POD HD500X Edit. Mac Line 6 POD HD500X Edit.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".DTS",
    "DTS Encoded Audio File",
    "3.1",
    "Multi-channel audio file encoded in the Digital Theater Systems (DTS) format; saves five tracks of audio data used for surround sound; channels include center, left-front, right-front, left-rear, and right-rear. NOTE: In order to play all channels of a DTS file, the output and speaker setup must support 5 channel audio. For example, this may be accomplished by using an optical out connection with a surround speaker system. Windows File Viewer Plus. VideoLAN VLC media player. CyberLink PowerDVD 21. Media Player Classic. Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. Macgo Mac Media Player. Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Linux VideoLAN VLC media playerFree. A DTS file is a device tree (or devicetree) source file. It contains plain text data that describes a computers hardware. DTS files are meant to be compiled into.DTB files, which are used by the Linux kernel. DTS file open in Microsoft Visual Studio Code Device trees are files that an operating systems kernel, or core program, uses to manage and communicate with the computers hardware. Because different computers contain different hardware, they use different device trees. A DTS file is the source file used to create a computers device tree. It contains a list of nodes, properties, and child nodes that describes what hardware a computer contains. For example, a DTS file describes the computers CPU, memory, buses, and peripherals (such as the computers keyboard). DTS files are compiled into DTB (Device Tree Blob) files, which are binary files that a computer uses during the booting process. DTS files are compiled using a DTC, or device tree compiler. Because DTS files are plain text files, you can open and edit them in any text editor, including GitHub Atom (cross-platform), GNU Emacs (cross-platform), and Vim (Linux). How do I compile a DTS file into a DTB file? To compile a DTS file into a DTB file, you must invoke Linuxs device tree compiler. The device tree compiler is stored in linux-xlnx/​scripts/​dtc and must itself be compiled to be used. After compiling the DTC, you can invoke it using the dtc command. For example, to compile a DTS file into a DTB file, you can enter the command dtc -I dts -O dtb -o filename.dtb filename.dts. Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor Linux Vim. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor Chrome OS Google Chrome Text Included with OS.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus. VideoLAN VLC media player. CyberLink PowerDVD 21. Media Player Classic. Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. Macgo Mac Media Player. Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. Linux Vim. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. Chrome OS Google Chrome Text Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".ALL",
    "Cubasis Project File",
    "3.1",
    "Security policy file used by Java RMI-enabled technologies such as Apache River (formerly Jini) and GigaSpaces; stores data access permissions and allows all entities full permissions; often used for development configurations, where developers are in a secure environment. The policy file giving all permissions usually has the name policy.all. The file is specified as a parameter when invoking a Java RMI application: java -Djava.security.policy=policy.all.. NOTE: RMI stands for Remote Method Invocation. This technology is used for creating distributed applications. Windows Apache River —  (Discontinued). GigaSpaces. Mac Apache River —  (Discontinued). GigaSpaces. Linux Apache River —  (Discontinued). GigaSpaces. Multi-track audio project file created by Steinberg Cubasis or early versions of Cubase VST; contains all the project data, which may include both audio and MIDI tracks. ALL projects can be opened by some versions of the Cubase VST and SL/SX software editions. Windows Steinberg Cubase. Steinberg Cubasis Mac Steinberg Cubase. Steinberg Cubasis.",
    "Windows Apache River —  (Discontinued). GigaSpaces. Mac Apache River —  (Discontinued). GigaSpaces. Linux Apache River —  (Discontinued). GigaSpaces. Windows Steinberg Cubase. Steinberg Cubasis. Mac Steinberg Cubase. Steinberg Cubasis.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".PEAK",
    "Steinberg Peak File",
    "3.1",
    "Contains the waveform image of a corresponding Cubase audio file; used for visually displaying the audio data within the Cubase track window; generated automatically when an audio file is recorded or imported into Cubase. PEAK files are saved by default in the Images folder within the current project folder. If they are deleted, Cubase will recreate the files when the associated audio files are accessed. NOTE: PEAK files store only the waveform image and do not contain any audio data. Windows Steinberg Cubase. Mac Steinberg Cubase.",
    "Windows Steinberg Cubase. Mac Steinberg Cubase.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".CFA",
    "Adobe Conformed Audio File",
    "3.1",
    "A CFA file is a data capture file created by Frontline ComProbe analyzers, such as the BPA 600 Dual Mode Bluetooth Protocol Analyzer and the BPA Low Energy Bluetooth Protocol Analyzer. It contains data collected by an analyzer such as the frame number, command, segment, block, or UUID. CFA files are collected by analyzers to determine if a product meets Bluetooth interoperability standards. ComProbe analyzers are used to decode all types of traffic including data packets, advertising packets, and LL control packets. Hundreds of companies around the world, such as Broadcom, Apple, Samsung, Nokia, Sony, Panasonic, and Toshiba, use these analyzers to analyze their products. You can open, analyze, and interpret CFA files with the free ComProbe Protocol Analysis System (CPAS) software. You can also open CFA files with the open-source Wireshark software. Windows Frontline ComProbe Analysis SystemFree. A CFA file is a cached audio file created by several Adobe software programs, including After Effects, Premiere Pro, and Encore. It contains audio data that has been conformed to a proprietary Adobe format. CFA files are used for improving the softwares performance when processing audio data and when generating audio waveform previews. When importing audio data, the software transforms the audio into a format that can be quickly processed by the software. This removes the need for the audio to be reprocessed each time it is used. However, due to the caching, there may be a delay the first time audio is imported. CFA files may become very large in size. You can turn off the caching option within Adobe applications, but the processing time for audio previews may increase. CFA files are actually created by Adobe Media Encoder, a standalone software component that is included with programs such as Adobe After Effects, Premiere Pro, and Encore. All such programs reference the same audio cache. Windows Adobe Audition 2023. Adobe After Effects 2023. Adobe Premiere Pro 2023. Adobe Encore CS6. Mac Adobe Audition 2023. Adobe After Effects 2023. Adobe Premiere Pro 2023. Adobe Encore CS6.",
    "Windows Frontline ComProbe Analysis System. Windows Adobe Audition 2023. Adobe After Effects 2023. Adobe Premiere Pro 2023. Adobe Encore CS6. Mac Adobe Audition 2023. Adobe After Effects 2023. Adobe Premiere Pro 2023. Adobe Encore CS6.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".SONG",
    "AudioSauna Song File",
    "3.1",
    "A SONG file is a song created by AudioSauna, a free online music production studio. It contains an audio project which includes bass, electro, and organ sounds along with synthesizer settings. SONG files can be exported as.WAV files. AudioSauna can be opened in a web browser meaning you do not have to download the software to use it. The interface consists of a virtual analog synthesizer that can be used to create songs and loops by adding sounds from presets and altering the settings. You can modify the volume, frequency, and speed, apply distortion effects, and more. Web Naive Solutions AudioSaunaFree.",
    "Web Naive Solutions AudioSauna.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".VCE",
    "Yamaha Voice File",
    "3.1",
    "A VCE file is an exam created with Visual CertExam Suite, which includes both Visual CertExam Designer and Visual CertExam Manager. It contains a list of questions and answer possibilities that can be compiled into a certification exam. You can open VCE files in Visual CertExam Suite, which is used for creating and delivering tests for IT certification. The Visual CertExam Designer tool allows you to create and edit exams and Visual CertExam Manager enables you to take the exams. NOTE: You can also upload VCE files to VCEConvert.com and convert them to.PDF files using the VCE to PDF online conversion tool. Windows Visual CertExam Suite. Web VCEConvert.com VCE to PDF. Voice or instrument used by Yamaha PSR keyboards, such as PSR S910; contains sound settings saved in the MIDI format; different types include bass, brass, guitar, choir, organ, piano, strings, and flute. VCE files can be loaded by a compatible Yamaha keyboard using a USB connection or memory card. When the file is loaded, it changes the settings of the voice. NOTE: The VCE files are no longer used in the latest Yamaha software releases. Most MIDI sequencers, such as Audacity and Cubase, support the VCE file extension. Windows Audacity. Steinberg Cubase. Mac Audacity. Steinberg Cubase. Linux AudacityFree.",
    "Windows Visual CertExam Suite. Web VCEConvert.com VCE to PDF. Windows Audacity. Steinberg Cubase. Mac Audacity. Steinberg Cubase. Linux Audacity.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".DLS",
    "Downloadable Sounds File",
    "3.1",
    "Roland GS MIDI sound set; based in the Interactive Music Architecture; contains sounds that can be played back using a MIDI input device. Windows FMJ-Software Awave Studio. Mac SimpleSynth.",
    "Windows FMJ-Software Awave Studio. Mac SimpleSynth.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".BCSTM",
    "BCSTM Audio Stream File",
    "3.1",
    "A BCSTM file is an audio file used by various Nintendo 3DS games. It contains audio such as a sound effect or background music that is looped during gameplay. BCSTM files must be transported to a PC before they can be opened by programs such as BrawlBox or foobar2000. BrawlBox can be used to convert BCSTM files to the more common.WAV file format. BCSTM files can also be created from WAV,.MP3,.OGG, or.FLAC files using Brawl Custom Song Maker. The BCSTM file typically is never accessed by the average user. It is most likely only seen by users looking to modify 3DS gameplay and change the audio. Windows BrawlBox. Foobar2000Free.",
    "Windows BrawlBox. Foobar2000.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".EAC3",
    "Dolby Digital Plus Audio",
    "3.0",
    "An EAC3 file is an audio file saved using enhanced AC-3 (EAC-3) compression. It contains compressed, multi-channel digital audio. EAC3 files are the successors to.AC3 files. Enhanced AC-3, also known as Dolby Digital Plus, is an audio codec Dolby Labs developed for the transport and storage of multi-channel digital audio. EAC-3 is an iteration of the original AC-3 codec, which was also known as Dolby Digital. While AC-3 supports up to six channels of audio, EAC-3 supports up to 15.1. Typically, EAC-3 compressed files are used as the audio tracks on Blu-ray and HD DVD movies. The EAC-3 codec, and EAC3 files, were designed to provide quality, movie theater-style sound in a variety of environments. You may also encounter EAC-3 audio within.MKV and.EVO files. You can open and play EAC3 files in a variety of media players, including VideoLAN VLC media player (cross-platform), Apple QuickTime Player (Mac), and Microsoft Windows Media Player (Windows). You can also use FFmpeg (cross-platform) to convert EAC3 files to more-common audio formats. Windows VideoLAN VLC media player. Microsoft Windows Media Player Included with OS. MPlayer. CyberLink PowerDVD 21. FFmpeg. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. MPlayer. FFmpeg. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. MPlayer. FFmpegFree.",
    "Windows VideoLAN VLC media player. Microsoft Windows Media Player Included with OS. MPlayer. CyberLink PowerDVD 21. FFmpeg. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. MPlayer. FFmpeg. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. MPlayer. FFmpeg.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".6CM",
    "Six Channel Module",
    "3.0",
    "6 channel audio file created by Starbreeze Studios Fasttracker. Windows Starbreeze Studios Fasttracker 2Free.",
    "Windows Starbreeze Studios Fasttracker 2.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".M2",
    "PC-98 Game Music File",
    "3.0",
    "3D model format used by World of Warcraft, an online multiplayer adventure game; describes the vertices, faces, textures, materials, and animation capabilities of a single model; used for players, creatures, and doodads (decoration objects) within the game. M2 files include a global texture list, global vertex list, LOD (level of detail) settings, global bounding units, global sequences, a skeleton, and visual effects. Windows Blizzard World of Warcraft. Mac Blizzard World of Warcraft. Sound file format used by Japanese PC-98 computers with the PMD FM sound driver and PC-98 audio emulators, such as FMPMD2000; contains music that was used by original PC-98 computer games. NOTE: In order to play M2 files with FMPMD2000, you need to download the WinFMP.dll and PMDWin.dll files, which are available from the same location. Windows FMPMD2000Free.",
    "Windows Blizzard World of Warcraft. Mac Blizzard World of Warcraft. Windows FMPMD2000.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".TMC",
    "Theta Music Composer 1.x Audio File",
    "3.0",
    "Audio file created by Theta Music Composer (TMC), a music editor for Atari; supports mono and stereo audio; allows users to experiment with stereo Atari music; differs from the similar.TM8 format, which supports 8 channels. TMC files can be played with ASAP - Another Slight Atari Player. Windows Another Slight Atari Player. Theta Music ComposerFree.",
    "Windows Another Slight Atari Player. Theta Music Composer.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".SERATO-STEMS",
    "Serato Studio Stems File",
    "3.0",
    "A SERATO-STEMS file is a data file created by Serato Studio, a digital audio workstation (DAW). Studio uses SERATO-STEMS files to separate audio tracks into distinct components, including vocals, melody, bass, and drums. Studio stores each SERATO-STEMS file in the same directory as the audio file with it is used. Music producers use Serato Studio to mix samples and other audio tracks together into finished songs. Studio includes a feature called Stems, which allows producers to quickly isolate elements of an imported audio track. For example, a producer could use Stems to isolate an audio tracks vocals and bass, allowing them to create a new sample using just those elements. When a producer uses the Stems feature on an audio track, Serato Studio creates a SERATO-STEMS file associated with that track. This file has the same filename as the audio track with which it is used, except that it uses the.serato-stems extension. The SERATO-STEMS file contains data that Serato Studio uses to isolate and selectively mute each of the audio tracks components. How to delete SERATO-STEMS files If you use Serato Studios Stems feature extensively, you may want to periodically delete your SERATO-STEMS files, to free up space on your computer. To find the SERATO-STEMS file associated with an imported audio file: Open Serato Studio and, in your library, select an audio file youve used with Stems. Press CTRL + R (Windows) or CMD + R (Mac) on your keyboard. The directory containing your audio file and its corresponding SERATO-STEMS file will appear. You can then right-click and delete the SERATO-STEMS file. SERATO-STEMS files are not meant to be manually opened. Serato Studio loads SERATO-STEMS files when you load their corresponding audio file. Windows Serato Studio. Mac Serato Studio.",
    "Windows Serato Studio. Mac Serato Studio.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".8MED",
    "Amiga OctaMED Music File",
    "3.0",
    "An 8MED file is a music file created by OctaMED, a sound tracker for the Commodore Amiga. It contains notes, pitches, and effects used to create music tracks and sound sequences. No known programs support 8MED files. In 1991, developer Teijo Kinnunen and publisher RBF Software released OctaMED, a follow-up to the popular MED sound tracker. While MED used only.MED files to store sounds, OctaMED used both MED and 8MED files to do the same. OctaMED was notable for being able to play eight-channel audio on the Commodore Amigas four-channel sound chip. While OctaMED was ported to Windows in the late 1990s (under the name MED Soundstudio), it is no longer developed or maintained. Because 8MED files are so old, no known programs currently support 8MED files. Both VLC media player and OpenMPT can play MED files, so its possible those programs may support 8MED files in the future. No programs available.",
    "No programs available.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".MWAND",
    "GarageBand MagicMentor Template",
    "3.0",
    "File containing interactive lessons in GarageBand; contains video that teaches the user to play instruments or learn chords; referenced by the program, user is typically unaware of its presence. Mac Apple GarageBand Included with OS.",
    "Mac Apple GarageBand Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".EVR",
    "Enhanced Variable Rate Audio File",
    "3.0",
    "Sound file compressed using the Enhanced Variable Rate Codec (EVRC); designed primarily for compressing speech with a low bitrate while maintaining high fidelity. The EVR codec can be applied to multiple types of audio files, including the 3GPP2 (.3G2) container format. It is used by some Qualcomm hardware devices and can be played back using RealPlayer software. Windows RealNetworks RealPlayer version 16 or earlier Mac RealNetworks RealPlayer version 16 or earlier.",
    "Windows RealNetworks RealPlayer version 16 or earlier. Mac RealNetworks RealPlayer version 16 or earlier.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".SDII",
    "Sound Designer 2 Audio File",
    "3.0",
    "Audio file formatted with the Sound Designer II standard, a mono and stereo audio format developed by Digidesign (now Avid); stores sample rate and bit depth data in addition to the audio data itself; commonly used for transferring audio data between digital audio workstation (DAW) applications. SDII is rarely used for Sound Designer II audio files. Use the.SD2 extension instead. Windows Avid Pro Tools. Mac Avid Pro Tools. Roxio Toast 20. Roxio Popcorn. Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Apple Logic Pro.",
    "Windows Avid Pro Tools. Mac Avid Pro Tools. Roxio Toast 20. Roxio Popcorn. Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Apple Logic Pro.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".HBS",
    "Line 6 POD HD Edit Setlist File",
    "3.0",
    "An HBS file is a template file created by Handlebars, a web template system. It contains a template written in HTML code and embedded with Handlebars expressions. An HBS file performs the same function as a.HANDLEBARS file. HBS file open in Atom Handlebars is a JavaScript library that helps developers create cleaner code. A Handlebars template includes a series of Handlebars expressions that look something like this: {{inputobject}}. By applying input code to HBS templates, Handlebars users can efficiently generate HTML code for use in their development projects. The Ember web app development framework also makes use of HBS templates. To deliver an HBS file to the browser, you must include it in the script tag, as shown below: <script id=entry-template type=text/x-handlebars-template> template content </script>. You can open and view an HBS file using any text editor. However, if you intend to edit the file, you should open the file using a source code editor, such as NotePad++ or Atom. These applications provide helpful source code editing tools and highlight the files syntax correctly. Mac Handlebars. Apple Xcode. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor Windows Handlebars. Notepad++. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor Linux Handlebars. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor. An HBS file is a set list created by Line 6 POD HD Edit, a DAW application that enables you to edit instrument sounds. It contains up to 64 presets that change the settings for FX, AMPS, Mixer, and Controllers, which customize the sound of your instrument. Once loaded, an HBS file will replace the currently loaded Set list within the application. To create the HBS file, customize your settings, select File → Save Setlist As.., name the file, choose the save location, and click Save. To open the H5S file, double-click the file or select File → Open Setlist.., navigate to the file, and click Open. In Windows, the default save location for H5B files is in the following directory: /​My Documents/​Line 6/​Tones/​POD HD Edit/​Setlists In Mac, the default save location for H5S files is in the following directory: /​Documents/​Line 6/​Tones/​POD HD Edit/​Setlists NOTE: The HBS extension was replaced by.H5S when POD HD500 Edit was released. Mac Line 6 POD HD500X Edit. Windows Line 6 POD HD500X Edit. An HBS file is a text file used by Haxball, an online physics-based multiplayer soccer game. It contains text in JSON5 format that describes a stadium, which includes how the camera views gameplay, team spawning points, player and ball physics, how objects collide, and the stadium background appearance. HBS files are typically used to upload and share stadiums that other Haxball players can play in. You can open HBS files with any text editor since the file stores JSON-formatted text. There are also several programs available that have been developed by players in the Haxball community that allow you to easily modify HBS files. However, the popular HaxPuck editor is not currently available. When users finish modifying a stadium stored in an HBS file, they typically upload it to the Community page on the Haxball site. Other users can then play soccer in that stadium. Mac Any text editor Windows Any text editor Linux Any text editor Web HaxballFree.",
    "Mac Handlebars. Apple Xcode. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor. Windows Handlebars. Notepad++. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor. Linux Handlebars. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor. Mac Line 6 POD HD500X Edit. Windows Line 6 POD HD500X Edit. Mac Any text editor. Windows Any text editor. Linux Any text editor. Web Haxball.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".AEA",
    "ATRAC1 Audio File",
    "3.0",
    "Contains settings for an alarm created with Ae Timer, an alarm clock and scheduling program; includes the alarm time, alarm text, and the song or video that is played for the alarm; can be edited and saved by the user. Windows Ae Applications Ae Timer. Backup archive created by Google AdWords Editor, an application used to manage information for Google AdWords advertising campaigns; contains the advertising data for the campaign; used for creating full or partial backups. AEA files may store data for an entire account or select Ad Groups and Campaigns. You can export one of these options by selecting File → Export Backup (AEA) and then choosing one of the submenu items. NOTE: AEA files are also used by Google Translator Toolkit, a browser-based application that can automatically translate the advertising campaign information into other languages. Windows Google AdWords Editor. Google Translator Toolkit —  (Discontinued). Mac Google AdWords Editor. Google Translator Toolkit —  (Discontinued). Linux Google Translator Toolkit —  (Discontinued). An AEA file contains audio data encoded in the ATRAC1 format, which is a data compression format developed by Sony. It stores audio most likely dumped from a MiniDisc (MD), which is an optical disc similar to a compact disc (CD) that can be played with various MD players. AEA files are not common, since MDs were introduced back in 1992 and overshadowed by CDs. You will most likely never encounter an AEA file unless you dump audio from an MD you own. You may also receive an AEA file from a friend sharing music dumped from one of his MDs. The ATRAC1 format is a variation of the ATRAC format, which stands for Adaptive TRansform Acoustic Coding. Besides being used in MDs, the format was also utilized in the Sony Dynamic Digital Sound (SDDS) theater sound system in the 1990s. Since AEA files are uncommon, there are few media players that support them. However, you can convert AEA files to a more widely supported audio format with FFmpeg, then play the converted file with a media player, such as Microsoft Windows Media Player or VideoLAN VLC media player. Unless the AEA file stores audio you cannot get anywhere else, such as a recorded narration or rare music recording, it is most likely easier to re-purchase or stream the audio from a digital music service than to convert it to a more common format that can be played. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. FFmpeg. Mac FFmpeg. Linux FFmpegFree.",
    "Windows Ae Applications Ae Timer. Windows Google AdWords Editor. Google Translator Toolkit —  (Discontinued). Mac Google AdWords Editor. Google Translator Toolkit —  (Discontinued). Linux Google Translator Toolkit —  (Discontinued). Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. FFmpeg. Mac FFmpeg. Linux FFmpeg.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".KTP",
    "Kinetic Project Template",
    "3.0",
    "Audio project template used by Kinetic, a program used for creating electronic music; saves instrument patches and audio loops that can be reused when creating new audio projects (.KIN files). NOTE: Cakewalk Kinetic is no longer being developed and was succeeded by Cakewalk SONAR. Windows Cakewalk SONAR X3.",
    "Windows Cakewalk SONAR X3.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".VB",
    "Grand Theft Auto Audio File",
    "3.0",
    "A VB file is a project item file written in the Visual Basic language, an object-oriented programming language created by Microsoft for use with the.NET Framework. It contains Visual Basic instructions in ASCII text format. A project item can refer to a variety of Visual Basic project components. Each available project item differs based on whether you are working in a local or web project. Examples of project items include a Windows form, Login form, splash screen, dialog, class, interface, code file, custom control, web custom control, or installer class. The vb extension is used for all of these items. Visual Basic is a programming language implemented on the.NET framework. Visual Basic.NET (VB.NET) was released in 2002 to replace the original Visual Basic language. The VB.NET language is used to create applications based on.NET, such as web applications and XML web services. .NET was eventually dropped by Microsoft in 2005 and the VB file is now used by Microsoft Visual Studio. NOTE: VB files can also be used to contain viruses or other malware. Therefore, do not open VB files if they are an unknown e-mail attachments. Windows File Viewer Plus. Microsoft Visual Studio 2022. Adobe Dreamweaver 2021. Microsoft WScript Included with OS. Any text editor Mac Adobe Dreamweaver 2021. Any text editor Linux Any text editor Android File Viewer for Android. Game ROM created from a Nintendo Virtual Boy video game; contains data from a Virtual Boy cartridge saved in a read-only file; can be played on a PC using a Virtual Boy emulation program such as Red Dragon. Virtual Boy was a portable game console developed by Nintendo and released in 1995. It included a headset that provided a 3D experience for gamers. Windows Red Dragon Reality Boy Virtual-E Mac OpenEmuFree. Audio file used by Grand Theft Auto (GTA) 3 and GTA: Vice City games for PlayStation 2; stores multiple audio clips and includes radio station clips, radio news clips, and cutscene audio; used for audio playback during gameplay. VB files can be converted to the.WAV format with MFAudio by setting the following program options: Frequency: 32000Hz, or 16000Hz for the talk stations (e.g., POLICE.VB, KCHAT.VB, and VCPR.VB) Samples: 16 bits Channels: 2 Interleave: 2000 Bytes Offset: 0 Bytes Output format: WAVE VB files are saved in the /​AUDIO/​ directory on the PlayStation 2 GTA disc. NOTE: VB audio files may also be used by the Windows versions of GTA3 and GTA: Vice City with the VBDec plugin installed. Windows MFAudio. VBDecFree. A VB file is a video used by a Beam Software video game. It contains a scene played within a game. VB files cannot be played by most popular media players. VB file open in VLC media player Beam Software is an Australian video game developer that was founded in 1978 and acquired by Krome Studios in 2006, at which point Beam was renamed Krome Studios Melbourne. In the 1990s, Beam produced a handful of games that use their proprietary SIFF file format, including KKND2: Krossfire and The Lost Vikings II. The SIFF file format can be used to create files that contain both audio and video or just audio. When a SIFF format file contains both audio and video, it is saved using the.vb extension. When it contains just audio, it is saved with the.SON extension. Because VB files are so uncommon, most popular media players cannot play them. However, you can play VB files in VLC media player, and you can convert them to a more usable video format using FFmpeg. Windows File Viewer Plus. VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpegFree.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus. Microsoft Visual Studio 2022. Adobe Dreamweaver 2021. Microsoft WScript Included with OS. Any text editor. Mac Adobe Dreamweaver 2021. Any text editor. Linux Any text editor. Android File Viewer for Android. Windows Red Dragon Reality Boy Virtual-E. Mac OpenEmu. Windows MFAudio. VBDec. Windows File Viewer Plus. VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".VGZ",
    "Video Game Music Compressed File",
    "3.0",
    "Video file recorded using a VGuard digital video card or a DigitalVDO security camera (CCTV) system; compressed using Super Motion Image Compression Technology (SMICT); can be played back using VG Player. Windows VG Player —  (Discontinued). Compressed audio file created to reduce the size of.VGM files; stores a Video Game Music (VGM) audio file compressed with.GZ compression; can be played with any VGM player that accepts the compressed format. VGZ files are used to store video game music used by older game systems such as the Sega Genesis and Sega Game Gear. Windows Audio Overload. Nullsoft Winamp with Chipamp plug-in. Mac Audio Overload. Cog. Linux Audio OverloadFree.",
    "Windows VG Player —  (Discontinued). Windows Audio Overload. Nullsoft Winamp with Chipamp plug-in. Mac Audio Overload. Cog. Linux Audio Overload.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".RMF",
    "Rich Music Format Audio File",
    "3.0",
    "Map file created by Valve Hammer Editor, a mapping tool included with the Valve Source SDK; contains Hammer data such as arbitrary brush shapes and VisGroups (Visibility Groups help you manage objects by giving you control of what you see on the screen); can be compiled into.MAP and.BSP files. To create a RMF file, simply select File → Save select the RMF format, and name your file. You can choose the save location of your RMF file but the default save location of RMF files created by Hammer Editor is in the Maps folder inside the Valve Hammer Editor folder. Windows Valve Hammer EditorFree. Audio file created in the Rich Music Format, an audio format created by Beatnik; used as a container format for MIDI files and other standard audio formats; can be encrypted to protect original music; used by some older video games. The Beatnik Editor, the original RMF editor released by Beatnik, is no longer available. However, the RMF format is still supported by Java Sound and the Java Media Framework. Windows Oracle Java Sound. The Beatnik Editor Mac Oracle Java Sound. The Beatnik Editor. License key file used by Adobe products such as Acrobat and Reader; saves a license file for a locked.PDF document and uses the same filename prefix as the PDF; allows the PDF to be read by the purchaser of the document. RMF files are sometimes distributed with purchases of eBooks and digital magazines purchased from onlines stores. Youll need the RMF file to open the corresponding PDF document. Windows Adobe Acrobat Reader DC. Adobe Acrobat DC. Mac Adobe Acrobat Reader DC. Adobe Acrobat DC.",
    "Windows Valve Hammer Editor. Windows Oracle Java Sound. The Beatnik Editor. Mac Oracle Java Sound. The Beatnik Editor. Windows Adobe Acrobat Reader DC. Adobe Acrobat DC. Mac Adobe Acrobat Reader DC. Adobe Acrobat DC.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".ST3",
    "Star 3 MIDI Karaoke File",
    "3.0",
    "An ST3 file is a compressed.MIDI file used by various computer karaoke programs, such as Star 3 and Real Orchestra. It contains music data in the MIDI format for how the instrumentation of a song is to be played. ST3 files also store the subtitle lyrics for a song, along with the artist and name of the song. ST3 files can be played with Star 3 and Real Orchestra programs. However, both of these programs have been discontinued. Windows Star 3 Real Orchestra.",
    "Windows Star 3 Real Orchestra.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".GBPROJ",
    "GarageBand Project",
    "3.0",
    "Audio project file created by GarageBand, a home audio production program; may contain MIDI data as well as recorded or imported audio tracks; used for saving music compilations during the production process. NOTE: GarageBand projects usually have the.BAND extension. Mac Apple GarageBand Included with OS.",
    "Mac Apple GarageBand Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".NAAC",
    "Namco AAC File",
    "3.0",
    "An NAAC file is an audio file used by Nintendo 3DS games developed by Namco, such as Ace Combat: Assault Horizon Legacy and Taiko no Tatsujin: Don to Katsu no Jikuu Daibouken. It stores compressed audio for a Namco 3DS game in the Advanced Audio Coding (AAC) format. NAAC files can be opened using vgmstream.  Windows vgmstream. Linux vgmstreamFree.",
    "Windows vgmstream. Linux vgmstream.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".DW",
    "David Whittaker Audio File",
    "3.0",
    "Audio File created to contain audio composed by David Whittaker for games on the Amiga operating system; used in Commodore Amiga games but can be played by specific players. DeliTracker was created in 1992 and played this file on the Amiga operating system, it ceased in 2000 but the DeliPlayer program was created to be emulated on the Windows operating system. Windows DeliPlayer. XMPlay. Linux Unix Amiga Delitracker Emulator (UADE)Free.",
    "Windows DeliPlayer. XMPlay. Linux Unix Amiga Delitracker Emulator (UADE).",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".SSEQ",
    "Synclavier Sequence File",
    "3.0",
    "An SSEQ file is an audio file saved in the Nintendo DS Sound Sequence (SSEQ) format. It is used by various games for the Nintendo DS, a portable game system that includes a touch screen. SSEQ files contain sounds and music for the game that are referenced for playback during gameplay. SSEQ files can be found within.SDAT Nintendo DS sound data files, which are stored within.NDS ROM files. SSEQ files can be converted to the.MID format using sseq2mid. The midi2sseq program can convert MID files to the SSEQ format. Windows sseq2mid midi2sseq. An SSEQ file is a sequence file created by Synclavier Digital SynclavierX, a digital synthesizer application. It contains musical information, such as notes played, instruments, and tempo, in the Synclavier Sequence (SSEQ) format. Synclavier Digital introduced the.sseq file extension as the file extension for its sequence files when it released version 3 of Synclavier in April 2015. The file extension replaced the.sq0data,.sq1data, etc. file extensions. If you have sequence files with these extensions, you can rename them with the.sseq file extension and open them in version 3 or later of Synclavier. To create an SSEQ sequence file with version 3 or later of Synclavier, select File → Save As.. After saving an SSEQ file, you can close it, then re-open it later to continue modifying the sequence. NOTE: Synclavier Digital discontinued SynclavierX. You can open an SSEQ file with Synclavier Digital SynclavierX in macOS. To open the SSEQ file with SynclavierX, select the SSEQ file in the Sound File Import window or click Sequence Files in the Synclavier Asset Library window, then select the SSEQ file you would like to open. Mac Synclavier Digital SynclavierX.",
    "Windows sseq2mid midi2sseq. Mac Synclavier Digital SynclavierX.",
    "Synclavier Digital SynclavierX can convert SSEQ files to the following formats:.AIFF - Audio Interchange File Format.CAF - Core Audio File.WAV - WAVE Audio File."],
    ["audio_files",
    ".PSF2",
    "PlayStation Sound Format File",
    "3.0",
    "Sound file created for sequenced music in Sony PlayStation 2 emulated games; contains samples, which are sounds (like a violin), and sequences, which indicate how the sounds should be played; resembles.PSF (Portable Sound File) files but created for PlayStation 2 games; structured as a file system, not a as a single executable like its predecessors. NOTE: The same as.PSF1 files except theyre created for PlayStation 2 games. Windows Audio Overload. Nullsoft Winamp with the Highly Experimental plugin. XMPlay with the Highly Experimental plugin. Mac Audio Overload. Linux Audio OverloadFree.",
    "Windows Audio Overload. Nullsoft Winamp with the Highly Experimental plugin. XMPlay with the Highly Experimental plugin. Mac Audio Overload. Linux Audio Overload.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".PSF1",
    "PlayStation Sound Format File",
    "3.0",
    "Audio file used for sequenced music in Sony PlayStation 1 emulated games; similar to.PSF (Portable Sound File) files but created for PlayStation games; contains samples, which are sounds (like a guitar), and sequences, which indicate how the sounds should be played. NOTE: The same as.PSF2 files except theyre created for PlayStation 1 games. Windows Audio Overload. Nullsoft Winamp with the Highly Experimental plugin. XMPlay with the Highly Experimental plugin. Mac Audio Overload. Linux Audio OverloadFree.",
    "Windows Audio Overload. Nullsoft Winamp with the Highly Experimental plugin. XMPlay with the Highly Experimental plugin. Mac Audio Overload. Linux Audio Overload.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".XOPUS",
    "Exient OPUS File",
    "3.0",
    "An XOPUS file contains a raw Opus audio stream used by a game with the Exient XGS Engine, such as Angry Birds Go! or Angry Birds Transformers. It stores audio referenced by the game for music or sound effects. Opus is an audio coding format developed by the Xiph.Org Foundation. It is an open, royalty-free format that features lossy compression. iOS Rovio Angry Birds Transformers. Rovio Angry Birds Go!. Android Rovio Angry Birds Transformers. Rovio Angry Birds Go!.",
    "iOS Rovio Angry Birds Transformers. Rovio Angry Birds Go!. Android Rovio Angry Birds Transformers. Rovio Angry Birds Go!.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".GRO",
    "Allegro MIDI File",
    "3.0",
    "Bitmap image format sometimes referred to as a GROB (GRaphic Object Bitmap); used by Hewlett-Packard scientific calculators, such as the HP-48 and HP-49; used for storing graphs, charts, and other graphics created on the calculator. GRO files may be viewed on a computer using a supporting HP calculator emulator, such as Emu48. Mac Emu48. XnViewMP. Windows Emu48. XnViewMP. Newera Graphics Converter Pro. ASCII text file that defines audio in a MIDI representation; also contains note tracks, which specify display data for the audio; can be imported (and subsequently converted to other audio formats) using Audacitys File → Import MIDI.. option. Mac Audacity. Windows Audacity. Linux AudacityFree.",
    "Mac Emu48. XnViewMP. Windows Emu48. XnViewMP. Newera Graphics Converter Pro. Mac Audacity. Windows Audacity. Linux Audacity.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".ITS",
    "Impulse Tracker Sample",
    "3.0",
    "An ITS file is a sample used by Impulse Tracker, an audio-tracking program. It contains a PCM sample of a sound effect, voice, etc., in the Impulse Tracker Sample (ITS) format. ITS files also store sample metadata, such as the sample name and format version in which it is saved. Impulse Tracker is a free music tracker created by Jeffrey Lim and released in 1995. The music sequencing program allows you to create music from samples and instruments organized into tracks and modified by notes and effects. In addition, you can share and load ITS samples in Impulse Tracker to add them to your composition (saved in the.IT file). You can open an ITS file with Impulse Tracker (Windows), but the software is not actively developed and may not run on your operating system version. CocoModX (macOS) can also open ITI files but is discontinued. Windows Impulse Tracker —  (Discontinued). Mac CocoModX —  (Discontinued). Preference file that contains a list of file types that should be opened by Microsoft Internet Explorer (IE); file types and associations can be edited in Windows Explorer by selecting View→Options→File Types. Windows Microsoft Windows.",
    "Windows Impulse Tracker —  (Discontinued). Mac CocoModX —  (Discontinued). Windows Microsoft Windows.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".CDLX",
    "Adobe Audition CD Layout File",
    "3.0",
    "A CDLX file contains an audio CD layout created by Adobe Audition, an audio production application. It stores the layout of one or more audio tracks and associated metadata for burning the information to an audio CD. CDLX file open in Adobe Audition 2023 Audition is a digital audio workstation (DAW) designed for professional audio editing. You can use the software to create, mix, design, and restore audio for various types of media, including songs, podcasts, radio broadcasts, and video audio. Adobe introduced the CDLX format with Audition CS6 (version 5) in April 2012. CDLX supports audio from any format that Audition supports and can store up to 685.5 MB of audio data, which is roughly 78 minutes of playtime. How to create a CDLX file To create a CDLX file with Audition, select File → New → CD Layout. Then, after adding audio files to the CD layout and modifying the settings, select File → Save or Save As. You can only open CDLX files with Adobe Audition (multiplatform). To open a CDLX file with Audition, select File → Open. Windows Adobe Audition 2023. Mac Adobe Audition 2023. Library file used by ConceptDraw PRO, a business data diagramming tool; contains shapes or objects that can be used in a data visualization, such as a diagram or chart; saved in the XML format. To create the CDLX file, select File → Library → Save As.., name the file, choose the save location, select CDLX (ConceptDraw XML Libraries, *.cdlx) from the File Format drop down menu, and click Save. NOTE: The CDLX file is the same as the.CDL file except it stores data in the XML format instead of the Binary format. Windows CS Odessa ConceptDraw PRO. Mac CS Odessa ConceptDraw PRO.",
    "Windows Adobe Audition 2023. Mac Adobe Audition 2023. Windows CS Odessa ConceptDraw PRO. Mac CS Odessa ConceptDraw PRO.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".WYZ",
    "WYZTracker File",
    "3.0",
    "File used by WYZTracker, a program used to create chiptune audio files in a format used by older Amstrad CPC AY sound chips; stores a pattern of notes and effects; often used for creating video game music. NOTE: The WYZTracker user interface is written in Spanish. Windows WYZTrackerFree.",
    "Windows WYZTracker.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".HCA",
    "High Compression Audio File",
    "3.0",
    "An HCA file contains audio compressed in the High Compression Audio proprietary codec and saved in the ADX2 format, which is the second version of the ADX format developed by CRI Middleware. It is used to store compressed audio, typically background music, for various video games, such as Phantasy Star Online 2. HCA files are commonly bundled into an.ACB or.AWB audio package file. One significant improvement of the ADX2 format over the ADX format is that music tracks can be layered to play multiple tracks of music at the same time. The ADX2 format is developed by CRI Middleware, a Japanese company that specializes in audio and video software in the entertainment industry. Windows Phantasy Star Online 2.",
    "Windows Phantasy Star Online 2.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".2CH",
    "Super Audio CD Two-Channel Audio",
    "3.0",
    "A 2CH file is a two-channel audio file that was likely included on a Super Audio CD (SACD). It contains a song that was ripped from a Super Audio CD or downloaded from a digital music marketplace. 2CH files are stereo versions of associated.DFF files. Super Audio CD is a type of optical disc that Sony and Phillips developed to replace typical audio CDs. All SACDs contain audio saved in the Direct Stream Digital (DSD) audio format, which notably supports up to six audio channels. However, many SACDs also contain a normal CD layer, which includes the same audio remixed into a two-channel format. These two-channel audio files are saved as 2CH files. Each 2CH file is encoded using 16-bit pulse-code modulation and sampled at 44.1 kHz. Normal CD players can read and play a discs 2CH files, allowing users to play their SACDs in SACD and CD players. You can open a 2CH file and play the audio it contains with VideoLAN VLC media player (multiplatform) or Foobar2000 (Windows). When using Foobar2000, youll likely have to install a SACD plug-in, such as Super Audio CD Decoder, to play your 2CH file. Windows VideoLAN VLC media player. Foobar2000. Super Audio CD Decoder. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. iOS VideoLAN VLC media player. Android VideoLAN VLC media playerFree.",
    "Windows VideoLAN VLC media player. Foobar2000. Super Audio CD Decoder. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. iOS VideoLAN VLC media player. Android VideoLAN VLC media player.",
    "You can use VideoLAN VLC media player to convert the audio a 2CH file contains to the following formats:.MP3 - MP3 Audio.OGG - Ogg Vorbis Audio.FLAC -. Lossless Audio Codec.WAV - WAVE Audio."],
    ["audio_files",
    ".HBE",
    "Line 6 POD HD Edit Preset File",
    "3.0",
    "File archive compressed and encrypted with the HyperBac file compression utility; used primarily for compressing database files, including Oracle, MySQL, SQL Server, SharePoint, Sybase, IBM DB/2, and SAP BRBackup database formats; can provide up to a 90% reduction in required storage space. HBE files are similar to standard.HBC files, but are encrypted using AES encryption for file security. HyperBac uses an encryption key file to authenticate the user(s) that can open the file. Windows Red Gate SQL HyperBac —  (Discontinued). Preset file created by Line 6 POD HD Edit, a program that enables you to edit the sound of your guitar; contains settings that customize the sound of your guitar; located under FX, AMPS, Mixer, and Controllers in the application interface; different settings include tone, bass, treble, channel volume, parameters, speed, and tempo sync. To create the HBE file, customize your settings, select File → Save As.., name the file, choose the save location, and click Save. To open the HBE file, double-click the file or select File → Open, navigate to the file, and click Open. In Windows, the default save location for HBE files is in the following directory: /​My Documents/​Line 6/​Tones/​POD HD Edit In Mac, the default save location for HBE files is in the following directory: /​Documents/​Line 6/​Tones/​POD HD Edit NOTE: The HBE extension can be opened by later versions of the POD HD Edit application such as POD HD500 Edit. Windows Line 6 POD HD500X Edit. Mac Line 6 POD HD500X Edit.",
    "Windows Red Gate SQL HyperBac —  (Discontinued). Windows Line 6 POD HD500X Edit. Mac Line 6 POD HD500X Edit.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".MT2",
    "MadTracker 2 Module",
    "3.0",
    "An MT2 file is an audio module format used by the MadTracker 2 audio tracking program. It contains one or more audio samples, instruments, patterns, and notes that comprise the melody. MT2 files also store metadata, including the version and title of the name and the tracker that created the module. MT2 file open in MadTracker 2 MadTracker 2 is a music sequencing application for creating music. It comes with various features, including built-in effects, VST plugins, samples, and demo songs. How to create an MT2 file You can create an MT2 file with MadTracker 2 by following these steps: Select File → New → MadTracker module Compose the music Select File → Save or Save As.. You can open an MT2 file with several applications, including MadTracker 2 and Schism Tracker. To open an MT2 file with MadTracker 2, select File → Open.. Windows MadTracker 2. Schism Tracker. Winamp with the MadTracker Player plugin Mac Schism Tracker. Linux Schism TrackerFree.",
    "Windows MadTracker 2. Schism Tracker. Winamp with the MadTracker Player plugin. Mac Schism Tracker. Linux Schism Tracker.",
    "MadTracker 2 can convert an MT2 file to the following formats:.WAV - WAVE Audio.MIDI - MIDI Music Data.OGG - Ogg Vorbis Audio To convert an MT2 file with MadTracker 2, select File → Export."],
    ["audio_files",
    ".GIG",
    "Tascam GigaSampler File",
    "3.0",
    "Sound sample format used by Tascam GigaSampler, a sampling program that produces realistic instrument voices and other sounds. GigaSampler was discontinued and replaced with GigaStudio. Windows Tascam GigaStudio. LinuxSampler. LMMS. Mac LMMS. Linux LinuxSampler. LMMSFree.",
    "Windows Tascam GigaStudio. LinuxSampler. LMMS. Mac LMMS. Linux LinuxSampler. LMMS.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".SCS11",
    "Show Cue System Cue File",
    "3.0",
    "XML file created by Show Cue System (SCS) 11, a program used for playing music and sound effect cues during live theatre performances; saves an ordered list of audio files, each of which can be played when triggered by the user. SCS11 files store descriptive information about each audio file that helps the live show audio engineer know what the sounds contain. SCS11 files can also store hotkey shortcuts that play certain sounds when triggered. This is useful for impromptu or commonly used sounds. NOTE: SCS11 files do not store actual audio data, but instead store references to the audio files. Therefore, you need to make sure to transfer all referenced audio files with the SCS11 file to successfully move the project to another computer. Windows Show Cue System.",
    "Windows Show Cue System.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".KSC",
    "Korg Trinity/Triton Script File",
    "3.0",
    "Contains a list of.KMP files, or multisamples, which reference audio samples; used by custom instruments created by the user; references audio files, but does not contain actual audio data. Windows FMJ-Software Awave Studio.",
    "Windows FMJ-Software Awave Studio.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".M5P",
    "MachFive Preset File",
    "3.0",
    "An M5P file is a preset used by MachFive, a sampler for music production. It contains a preset, which is an instrument or effect used by MachFive as the main unit for creating compositions. MachFive comes with presets included but you can also load presets into the program. You can use th presets to produce performances, which are stored in M5M files. M5P presets that come with the application are located in the Preset folder. You may see the M5P file in this folder but you will most likely come across the file when receiving the file from another user or website to load into the program. Windows MOTU MachFive. Mac MOTU MachFive.",
    "Windows MOTU MachFive. Mac MOTU MachFive.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".CONFORM",
    "Conformalizer Change List File",
    "3.0",
    "File exported by Conformalizer, an audio post production program used for conforming produced audio to a video; saves data for conforming input Pro Tools sessions, FX lists, or ADR databases to a picture cut; incorporates a change Edit Decision List (.EDL) and associated metadata. NOTE: Maggot Software was acquired by The Cargo Cult. Mac The Cargo Cult Conformalizer —  (Discontinued). Trial.",
    "Mac The Cargo Cult Conformalizer —  (Discontinued). Trial.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".FZV",
    "Casio FZ-1 Voice Dump",
    "3.0",
    "An FZV file is a voice (sound) dumped from a Casio FZ series electronic keyboard. It contains a tone played by a synthesized instrument, such as a flute, trumpet, or piano. Users can dump sounds as FZV files using the FZDUMP utility. FZV file open in FMJ-Software Awave Studio Musicians use Casio FZ series keyboards, including the FZ-1, FZ-10M, FZ-20M, to play synthesized electronic music. Each keyboard can contain up to 64 individual sounds, which may be organized into sound banks. If a musician wants to export and edit a sound their keyboard contains, they can do so using the FZDUMP Windows utility. FZDUMP saves individual sounds as FZV files. (It saves sound banks as.FZB files and entire sound libraries as.FZF files.). To play an FZV file, open it in FMJ-Software Awave Studio (Windows). To edit the sound an FZV file contains, open it in Casio FZ Librarian (Windows). To transfer an FZV file to a Casio FZ series keyboard, connect the keyboard to your PC and use FZDUMP (Windows) to transfer the file. Windows FMJ-Software Awave Studio. Casio FZ Librarian. FZDUMPFree.",
    "Windows FMJ-Software Awave Studio. Casio FZ Librarian. FZDUMP.",
    "Casio FZ Librarian and FMJ-Software Awave Studio can convert FZV files to other audio formats. Casio FZ Librarian can convert FZV files to the.WAV format. FMJ-Software Awave Studio can convert FZV files to many formats, including:.AAC - Advanced Audio Coding.AIFF - Audio Interchange File Format.AMR - Adaptive Multi-rate Codec.FLAC -. Lossless Audio Codec.IFF - Interchange File Format.M4A - MPEG-4 Audio.MP3 - MP3 Audio.OGG - Ogg Vorbis Audio.OPUS - Opus Audio.WAV - WAVE Audio."],
    ["audio_files",
    ".FZF",
    "Casio FZ-1 Full Voice Dump",
    "3.0",
    "An FZF file is a collection of voices (sounds) dumped from a Casio FZ series electronic keyboard. Users create FZF files using the FZDUMP utility. After dumping sounds to an FZF file, users can open the file on their PC with various FZ audio utilities. FZF file open in FMJ-Software Awave Studio Released in the late 1980s and early 1990s, Casio FZ series electronic keyboards allow users to play music using synthesized sounds. The FZ series included the FZ-1, FZ-10M, and FZ-20M keyboards. The Hohner HS-1 is a rebranded FZ-1. FZ series users who want to modify the sounds their keyboard contains can do using FZDUMP. FZDUMP allows users to extract sounds from or send sounds to FZ series keyboards. When a user chooses to extract all the sounds from their keyboard, FZDUMP saves the resulting collection as an FZF file. In contrast,.FZB files contain a single sound bank, and.FZV files contain a single sound. At most, an FZF file can contain 64 sounds, as that is the maximum number of sounds an FZ series keyboard can store. If you want to play the sounds an FZF file contains, you can open it in FMJ-Software Awave Studio (Windows). If you want to edit the sounds an FZF file contains, or add additional sounds to the file, you can open it in Casio FZ Librarian (Windows). To transfer an FZF file to a Casio FZ series keyboard, you must connect the keyboard to your PC and use the FZDUMP utility (Windows) to transfer the file. Windows FMJ-Software Awave Studio. Casio FZ Librarian. FZDUMPFree.",
    "Windows FMJ-Software Awave Studio. Casio FZ Librarian. FZDUMP.",
    "Casio FZ Librarian and FMJ-Software Awave Studio can convert the sounds FZF files contain to other formats. Casio FZ Librarian can convert sounds to the.WAV format. FMJ-Software Awave Studio can convert sounds to many formats, including:.AAC - Advanced Audio Coding.AIFF - Audio Interchange File Format.AMR - Adaptive Multi-rate Codec.FLAC -. Lossless Audio Codec.IFF - Interchange File Format.M4A - MPEG-4 Audio.MP3 - MP3 Audio.OGG - Ogg Vorbis Audio.OPUS - Opus Audio.WAV - WAVE Audio."],
    ["audio_files",
    ".PCA",
    "Perfect Clarity Audio File",
    "3.0",
    "Audio format used by MAGIX Sound Forge Pro audio editing program; originally created by Sonic Foundry, which was bought by Sony then acquired by MAGIX. Windows MAGIX Sound Forge Pro 16. MAGIX ACID Pro 10. A PCA file is an archive of a Teamwork Draft (.PLC file) created with GRAPHISOFT Archicad architectural designing software. It stores all of the information of a Teamwork Project (.PLP file) hosted on BIMcloud that is instead stored on the users local machine. PCA files are similar to PLC files but are saved for backup or transfer purposes (they may or may not also be compressed to reduce their file size. GRAPHISOFT Archicad is building information modeling (BIM) software that architects often use to design the appearance of structures, such as homes, office buildings, and hotels. The app enables you to work remotely with a team of other Archicad users via its BIMcloud storage space. Via BIMcloud, you can create a Teamwork Project that each team member can edit. You can also save a draft of the teamwork project as a PLC file on your local machine, allowing you to edit the draft, then send it to the teamwork project when ready. If you want to back up the draft or transfer it to another machine, save it as a PCA file. You can only open PCA files with GRAPHISOFT Archicad in Windows and macOS. To open a PCA file, select File → Open. Windows Graphisoft Archicad. Mac Graphisoft Archicad.",
    "Windows MAGIX Sound Forge Pro 16. MAGIX ACID Pro 10. Windows Graphisoft Archicad. Mac Graphisoft Archicad.",
    "Graphisoft Archicad can convert PCA files to various file types, including the following formats:.PLC - Archicad Teamwork Draft.PLN - Archicad Solo Project.PLA - Archicad Project Archive.DWG - AutoCAD Drawing.DXF - Drawing Exchange Format.IFC - Industry Foundation Classes File.C4D - Cinema 4D Model.3DS - 3D Studio Scene.SKP - SketchUp Document.OBJ - Wavefront 3D Object File.STL - Stereolithography File.PDF - Portable Document Format.JPG - JPEG Image."],
    ["audio_files",
    ".MA1",
    "Monarch Audio File",
    "3.0",
    "Sound file encoded by Monarch Video Vision audio and video recording software, such as FireX and Digimix; used for mixing audio tracks in video production applications. Windows Monarch Digimix Monarch FireX.",
    "Windows Monarch Digimix Monarch FireX.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".WUT",
    "WUTG Tag File",
    "3.0",
    "WUTG tag without wrapped audio; includes ID3v1 tags, such as Artist, Album, Composer, etc, plus other WUTG tags; does not contain actual audio data. Windows WUSSoft WUTG Editor. A WUT file is an image used by the Wii U version of Angry Birds Trilogy. It contains a texture used to skin an in-game object. Players are not meant to open WUT files. Angry Birds Trilogy is a console re-release of the first three Angry Birds mobile games. Fun Labs developed the Wii and Wii U versions of Angry Birds Trilogy. The Wii U version of Angry Birds Trilogy uses textures saved as WUT files. These files are similar to the GTX files used by some other Wii U games. You can open a WUT file in Noesis (Windows), using the AboodXD WiiU library and a supporting Python script. You can find a link to the library and script below. Windows Noesis. Noesis WUT Format ScriptFree.",
    "Windows WUSSoft WUTG Editor. Windows Noesis. Noesis WUT Format Script.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".ESPS",
    "ESPS Sampled Data File",
    "3.0",
    "Proprietary audio format created by Entropic Research Laboratories and used for its WAVES+ display program, ESPS signal processing library and the HTK speech recognition toolkit. Windows The Hidden Markov Model Toolkit (HTK) FMJ-Software Awave Studio.",
    "Windows The Hidden Markov Model Toolkit (HTK) FMJ-Software Awave Studio.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".KOZ",
    "Audiokoz Music File",
    "3.0",
    "Song downloaded to a cell phone from Full Track Music; used by Bell Canada / Bell Mobile for phones such as the Sanyo MM-7500. Windows Playable only on a supported cell phone Mac Playable only on a supported cell phone. Audio format developed by Chaoticom and used by Groove Mobile for downloading songs to mobile phones; also used by the Sprint Music store for Sprint/Nextel subscribers. KOZ files can only be played on compatible cell phones and not on computers. However, a corresponding.WMA file, which is playable on a PC, is usually made available as a free download with the KOZ file. These files can be played with Microsoft Windows Media Player. Windows Not meant to be opened on a computer Mac Not meant to be opened on a computer.",
    "Windows Playable only on a supported cell phone. Mac Playable only on a supported cell phone. Windows Not meant to be opened on a computer. Mac Not meant to be opened on a computer.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".KOZ",
    "Bell Music File",
    "3.0",
    "Song downloaded to a cell phone from Full Track Music; used by Bell Canada / Bell Mobile for phones such as the Sanyo MM-7500. Windows Playable only on a supported cell phone Mac Playable only on a supported cell phone. Audio format developed by Chaoticom and used by Groove Mobile for downloading songs to mobile phones; also used by the Sprint Music store for Sprint/Nextel subscribers. KOZ files can only be played on compatible cell phones and not on computers. However, a corresponding.WMA file, which is playable on a PC, is usually made available as a free download with the KOZ file. These files can be played with Microsoft Windows Media Player. Windows Not meant to be opened on a computer Mac Not meant to be opened on a computer.",
    "Windows Playable only on a supported cell phone. Mac Playable only on a supported cell phone. Windows Not meant to be opened on a computer. Mac Not meant to be opened on a computer.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".SEQUENCE",
    "Online Sequencer Sequence",
    "3.0",
    "A SEQUENCE file is a song created by Online Sequencer, a web-based music sequencer. It contains a collection of sequenced musical notes. SEQUENCE files also contain song metadata, such as the songs time signature, instrument settings, grid spacing, and other data. SEQUENCE file open in Online Sequencer Online Sequencer is a music sequencer that musicians can access in their web browser, at onlinesequencer.net. It allows musicians to place notes upon a grid to create a song. While creating a song, musicians can also adjust the songs time signature, BPM, playback instrument, and other settings. After creating a song, musicians can choose to save the song online or download it to their computer. Downloaded songs are saved as SEQUENCE files. Musicians can also download other users songs as SEQUENCE files from the Sequences section of Online Sequencers website. You can open a SEQUENCE file with Online Sequencer (Web). To do so: Select the three-dots menu button that appears on Online Sequencers right-hand side. Select Upload Sequence File. Navigate to and open your SEQUENCE file. Web Online SequencerFree.",
    "Web Online Sequencer.",
    "You can use Online Sequencer to convert SEQUENCE files to the following formats:.MP3 - MP3 Audio.WAV - WAVE Audio.MID - MIDI File To do so, choose the Show options button that appears next to the Save icon. Then, choose the format in which you want to export your SEQUENCE file."],
    ["audio_files",
    ".FDP",
    "FMOD Project File",
    "3.0",
    "Encrypted file or folder used to protect important files; only accessible using fingerprint reader authentication. Windows UPEK Protector Suite QL. Project file created by FMOD, a sound design tool used for authoring game sounds; saves the design for audio events, which are sounds (i.e., footsteps, explosions, and ambient sounds) that can be invoked in the games program code; allows the sounds to be programmatically triggered and customized while the game is running, which creates a more immersive gameplay environment. An FMOD project is built into an FMOD Events (.FEV) file and an FMOD Sound Bank (.FSB) file. These two files are used by the game runtime to trigger and play audio events. NOTE: FDP files were replaced by FSPRO files when FMOD Designer was renamed FMOD Studio. However, FDP files can still be opened by FMOD Studio. Windows Firelight Technologies FMOD Studio. Mac Firelight Technologies FMOD Studio.",
    "Windows UPEK Protector Suite QL. Windows Firelight Technologies FMOD Studio. Mac Firelight Technologies FMOD Studio.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".DPDOC",
    "Digital Performer Project",
    "3.0",
    "A DPDOC file is a project file created by MOTU Digital Performer, an audio editing and production program. It organizes and links to the audio files included in a Digital Performer audio project. In Digital Performer, DPDOC files appear primarily as timelines comprised of one or more audio tracks. DPDOC file open in MOTU Digital Performer MOTU Digital Performer is a digital audio workstation (DAW) that allows audio producers to edit, mix, record, play back, and export audio. When producers create a new project in Digital Performer, that project is saved within a DPDOC file. DPDOC files do not, themselves, contain any audio. Instead, they contain references to the audio files used in a Digital Performer project. Typically, Digital Performer imports and stores audio files referenced in DPDOC files in its Audio Files folder. DPDOC files also contain a record of the edits made to a project and the audio sequences included in that project. If you want to load the sequences contained within one DPDOC file into another Digital Performer project, you can do so by selecting File → Load from Digital Performers menu bar. This will allow you to select a DPDOC file from which to import sequences, as well as the sequences you want to import. NOTE: While MOTU Digital Performer was initially available for only macOS, it is now available for both macOS and Windows. You can open a DPDOC file in MOTU Digital Performer (Windows, Mac). To do so, open Digital Performer and select File → Open from the programs menu bar. Windows MOTU Digital Performer. Mac MOTU Digital Performer.",
    "Windows MOTU Digital Performer. Mac MOTU Digital Performer.",
    "You can use MOTU Digital Performer to convert the audio project a DPDOC file contains to the following formats:.MID - MIDI File.AAF - Advanced Authoring Format.OMF - Open Media Framework.XML - XML File To do so, select File → Export. Then, select your desired export format."],
    ["audio_files",
    ".RNG",
    "Nokia Composer Ringtone",
    "3.0",
    "Monophonic ringtone format used by Nokia cell phones; can be created using the Nokia Composer program included with certain Nokia phones; because it is a monophonic format, only one note can be played at a time. Windows Audio-Ware Ringtone Converter. File used for validating.XML documents; uses a simple schema language for XML that focuses on the description and validation of the structure and content of an XML document. Windows SyncRO Soft oXygen XML Editor. Apache OpenOffice. Mac SyncRO Soft oXygen XML Editor. Apache OpenOffice. Linux SyncRO Soft oXygen XML Editor. Apache OpenOfficeFree.",
    "Windows Audio-Ware Ringtone Converter. Windows SyncRO Soft oXygen XML Editor. Apache OpenOffice. Mac SyncRO Soft oXygen XML Editor. Apache OpenOffice. Linux SyncRO Soft oXygen XML Editor. Apache OpenOffice.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".RPL",
    "Dolby Cinema Print Master File",
    "3.0",
    "An RPL file is a match replay recorded by Toribash, a multiplatform fighting game developed by Nabi Studios. It contains a (plain text) record of everything that occurred during a match, including the fighters movements and the final score. Players can create RPL files at the end of a match by pressing F on their keyboard. In Toribash, players control the joints of stick-figure-like characters to create custom fighting moves. Players can play against the games AI or other players. They can also practice their moves in free play modes. If a player wants to save a replay of their match or free play session, they can do so by pressing F at the end of the session. Toribash then saves a record of the session as an RPL file. Each RPL file contains plain text data that Toribash uses to replay the match or free play session it describes. Players can share RPL files with each other so they can watch and edit each others replays. (To edit a replay, press E while the replay is playing.) Where does Toribash save RPL files? Toribash typically saves RPL files in its ~/​Toribash/​replay directory. For example, the Windows Steam version of Toribash saves RPL files to the following directory: C:/​Program Files (x86)/​Steam/​steamapps/​common/​Toribash/​replay. You can open an RPL file in Toribash (multiplatform). To do so, place the file in your ~/​Toribash/​replay directory. Then, open Toribash and select Setup → Replays. You should be able to select and play the replay your RPL file contains. You can also open an RPL file in any text editor, to view the plain text data it contains. Windows Nabi Studios Toribash. Any text editor Mac Nabi Studios Toribash. Any text editor Linux Nabi Studios Toribash. Any text editor. Game replay file created by Special Force, an online first-person shooter game; saves a first-person perspective video captured during gameplay; sometimes used to submit replays of cheaters to game authorities. RPL files are saved to the C:/​Program Files/​DFIGAMES/​Dragonfly/​Special Force/​Data/​Save/​ directory. NOTE: DF Interactive Special Force has been discontinued. Windows DF Interactive Special Force. An RPL file contains video data encoded with the ESCAPE codec and uncompressed or compressed audio data stored in the ARMovie multimedia container format. It is used in various computer games including Big Red Racing and the Tomb Raider series. RPL files are primarily used for saving replays of gameplay. All of the games that utilize RPL files are discontinued, with most of them being released in the 1990s. Since the files are no longer used to save replays you will most likely only encounter them if you have installed one of these older Eidos-developed PC games. The RPL files all utilize the same multimedia container but may store video encoded in different variations of the ESCAPE codec. The variations include ESCAPE 122, 124, and 130. NOTE: Eidos Interactive was acquired by Square Enix in 2009. There are few programs that support RPL files since they are rarely used. However, you can open and convert RPL files to more common video formats with FFmpeg, then open the converted file with a media player, such as Microsoft Windows Media Player or VLC media player. Windows File Viewer Plus. FFmpeg. Mac FFmpeg. Linux FFmpegFree. An RPL file is a cinema print master file created using Dolby Atmos Monitor and a Dolby Rendering and Mastering Unit, a professional sound rendering system that is made available to only select, cinema-grade filmmakers. It contains audio that is designed to be included in a film that will be played in a Dolby Atmos theater. RPL files can also be played back in the commercially-available Dolby Atmos Mastering Suite and Dolby Atmos Production Suite, using Dolby Atmos Renderer. Dolby provides certain filmmakers and studios with a specially-licensed computer that is designed specifically to let sound engineers and designers create cinema-grade Dolby Atmos audio tracks. These computers, called Dolby Rendering and Mastering Units, are controlled from a secondary PC using Avid Pro Tools, a separately-licensed digital audio workstation, and the Dolby Atmos Monitor. The Monitor is used to condense all the audio files and other information included within a movies Pro Tools project into one master audio track, which is saved with the.rpl extension. This RPL file is then included within a movie before that movie is shipped to and played at Dolby Atmos theaters. While non-cinema-level filmmakers cannot create RPL files, they can play them. Dolbys commercially-available Atmos Mastering Suite and Atmos Production Suite can both play RPL files, using the Dolby Atmos Renderer included within those suites. You can open and play an RPL file with Dolby Atmos Renderer, the audio rendering application included within the Dolby Atmos Mastering Suite and Dolby Atmos Production Suite. To do so, open the Renderer and select File → Open Master File. You can also convert an RPL file to a more usable format, such as WAV, with the Dolby Atmos Conversion Tool included within Dolby Atmos Mastering Suite. Mac Dolby Atmos Mastering Suite. Dolby Atmos Production Suite.",
    "Windows Nabi Studios Toribash. Any text editor. Mac Nabi Studios Toribash. Any text editor. Linux Nabi Studios Toribash. Any text editor. Windows DF Interactive Special Force. Windows File Viewer Plus. FFmpeg. Mac FFmpeg. Linux FFmpeg. Mac Dolby Atmos Mastering Suite. Dolby Atmos Production Suite.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".BWF",
    "Broadcast Wave File",
    "3.0",
    "Audio wave.WAV file with extra information, such as timestamps and other metadata, contained in the header. Windows Adobe Audition 2023. Cakewalk SONAR X3. Avid Pro Tools. Mac Adobe Audition 2023. Apple Logic Pro. Apple Final Cut Pro. Avid Pro Tools.",
    "Windows Adobe Audition 2023. Cakewalk SONAR X3. Avid Pro Tools. Mac Adobe Audition 2023. Apple Logic Pro. Apple Final Cut Pro. Avid Pro Tools.",
    "?"],
    ["audio_files",
    ".RCD",
    "KaiOS Audio",
    "3.0",
    "Recording created by pcAnywhere remote desktop control software; stores a screen recording of the remote desktop environment as it is being used; may include multiple sessions in a single file; can be used for technical support logs. RCD files are saved in a proprietary format and can only be played using the pcAnywhere software. NOTE: If you want to convert an RCD file to a standard video format such as.MPG or.AVI, one option is to use a separate screen recording software and record your screen as the RCD file is played back in pcAnywhere. Windows Symantec pcAnywhere —  (Discontinued). File created by LEGO MINDSTORMS NXT robot programming software; records positions of a physical LEGO MINDSTORMS robot in sequence by taking samples at a high frequency; allows users to create and replay robot movements; saved with the filename RobotAction.rcd by default. RCD files can be played on Android mobile devices with the MINDdroid app. NOTE: LEGO MINDSTORMS NXT evolved into LEGO MINDSTORMS EV3 in 2013. Windows LEGO MINDSTORMS NXT. Mac LEGO MINDSTORMS NXT. Android LEGO MINDdroidFree. An RCD file is used by Arcade, a program created for modeling physical structures in real-time using computer game computational methods. RCD files are used to create dynamic physical simulations in educational environments for teaching exercises, homework, and labs. Arcade was developed by the University of Virginia and distributed freely. Windows Arcade. An RCD file is an audio recording created by a mobile phone that uses the KaiOS operating system. It contains audio recorded using the phones Recorder app. RCD files are stored in a phones Audio folder. KaiOS is an Android-based operating system used by several models of feature phones, which are old-style, button-based cell phones that allow users to install and access simple applications. Notably, the Nokia 8110 and Alcatel MyFlip A405DL use the KaiOS operating system. By default, KaiOS includes a Recorder app that feature phone users can use to record audio memos. The app saves these audio files as RCD files, which are formatted similarly to.OGG audio files. RCD files are named using the time at which they were saved, with a filename that follows the format record_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.rcd. Most often, youll want to open and play RCD files using the Recorder app on your KaiOS mobile phone. However, if you want to play an RCD file on your computer, you can do so by transferring the file to your computer and opening it in VLC media player (cross-platform). Windows VideoLAN VLC Media Player. Mac VideoLAN VLC Media Player. Linux VideoLAN VLC Media PlayerFree.",
    "Windows Symantec pcAnywhere —  (Discontinued). Windows LEGO MINDSTORMS NXT. Mac LEGO MINDSTORMS NXT. Android LEGO MINDdroid. Windows Arcade. Windows VideoLAN VLC Media Player. Mac VideoLAN VLC Media Player. Linux VideoLAN VLC Media Player.",
    "?"],
