    "2.0",
    "File created by chipsounds, a program used to create sounds like those on older arcade machines, game consoles, and computers; stores the sound settings using XML formatting instead of the binary formatting used with.ARIA files. ARIAX files allow the sound designer to manually modify the sound using a text editor or an XML editor. Windows Plogue chipsounds. Mac Plogue chipsounds.",
