    ".NAP",
    "Napster Secured Music File",
    "1.0",
    "File used by McAfee ePolicy Orchestrator (ePO), a software product used for securing enterprise business networks; contains an extension for the ePO software; may include enhancements such as new scanning or reporting capabilities; also used for authorizing purchased software features. NOTE: McAfee ePolicy Orchestrator is now Trellix ePolicy Orchestrator. Windows Trellix ePolicy Orchestrator. Copy-protected music file from Napsters subscription-based music download service; developed jointly by Napster and Playmedia Systems as a secure music format; protects music copyrights by limiting the systems on which each file can be played. NAP files are similar to.M4P files downloaded from the iTunes music store, but use a different encoding. Windows Microsoft Windows Media Player Included with OS. Metafile that can be opened by several graphics applications, including the CorelDRAW Graphics Suite; contains vector graphics; used as a container for storing illustrations and other drawings. Windows CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023.",
